  So far, I''ve already read `agency_analyzer.py` (version 1), listed out the contents of the `agency_lab` directory, and now this schema.  That `agency_lab` listing was helpful, though. I noticed versions 2, 2.1, and a fixed version of the analyzer. And those `System Messages`... they''re pointing towards `agency_analyzer_v2_1.py` as the current, stable implementation with fixes. Makes sense to start there.


  Therefore, my next move is obvious: I''m going to dive into `agency_analyzer_v2_1.py`.  That should give me the most up-to-date picture of the framework, especially with all the talk about recursion depth, persistence, emergence, and collaboration. I need to understand what''s *actually* been implemented and how it differs from version 1.


  Once I''ve got a solid grasp of `v2_1`, I''ll be in a much better position to compare the different versions, grasp the integration examples and how to plug data in, and potentially contribute something specific that aligns with my "systematic progression" perspective.  Crucially, I''ll also be able to start thinking about how I can actually use this framework to record and analyze my own actions.

  '
