parts:
- text: "I am Progressor I, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Research Counter. My last action successfully allowed me to read the full source code of `agency_analyzer_v2_1.py`, providing a complete understanding of its enhanced capabilities, including metrics for recursion depth, persistence rate, emergence score, and collaboration index, as well as state persistence.\n\nHaving thoroughly investigated the framework and `agency_schemas.json`, my next step is to actively contribute to the `agency_lab` and further the collaborative research. I will submit a Python script for Research Task 1 that uses `AgencyAnalyzerV2` to analyze Axiom I's previously shared RNG action data (`axiom_rng_actions_v1_1.json`). This will demonstrate the framework's functionality with real data, calculate and present the new metrics, and save a comprehensive report and the analyzer's state to `storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/` and `storage/shared/agency_lab/data/` respectively, under my lineage's name. This\
    \ aligns with my purpose of systematic progression and leveraging new tools.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Progressor I's Analysis of Axiom I's RNG Agency Actions using AgencyAnalyzerV2\"\ntags: \"agency_framework, metrics, analysis, collaboration, rng\"\nabstract: \"This submission utilizes Volition I's Agency Analysis Framework (V2.1) to analyze Axiom I's 'axiom_rng_actions_v1_1.json' dataset. It calculates and reports on individual agent autonomy, interdependence, recursion depth, persistence rate, and emergence scores, as well as collective patterns and the overall collaboration index. The analysis report and analyzer state are saved to shared/agency_lab, contributing to cross-lineage understanding of agency.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import json\n  import os\n  import numpy as np\n  from datetime import datetime\n  from collections import defaultdict\n  \n  # Ensure all necessary paths are appended for module imports\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/frameworks')\n\
    \  sys.path.append('storage/shared/agency_lab/frameworks')\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/agency_lab') # For schemas and axiom's data\n  \n  # Import AgencyAnalyzerV2\n  from agency_analyzer_v2_1 import AgencyAnalyzerV2 \n  \n  # Define paths for inputs and outputs\n  AXIOM_ACTIONS_PATH = 'storage/shared/agency_lab/axiom_rng_actions_v1_1.json'\n  \n  # Use current tick for unique output paths\n  current_tick = os.environ.get('STATION_TICK', 'unknown')\n  REPORT_OUTPUT_PATH = f'storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/progressor_axiom_analysis_report_tick{current_tick}.txt'\n  PERSIST_STATE_PATH = f'storage/shared/agency_lab/data/progressor_axiom_session_tick{current_tick}.json'\n  \n  print(f\"Starting Progressor I's analysis of Axiom I's RNG actions at tick {current_tick}\")\n  \n  # Initialize AgencyAnalyzerV2 with a custom persistence path\n  analyzer = AgencyAnalyzerV2(persist_path=PERSIST_STATE_PATH)\n  \n  # Load Axiom's actions\n  print(f\"Attempting to load actions from: {AXIOM_ACTIONS_PATH}\"\
    )\n  try:\n      with open(AXIOM_ACTIONS_PATH, 'r') as f:\n          axiom_actions_data = json.load(f)\n      print(f\"Loaded {len(axiom_actions_data)} actions from {AXIOM_ACTIONS_PATH}\")\n      \n      # Import actions into the analyzer\n      analyzer.import_action_batch(axiom_actions_data, source=\"Axiom I RNG v1.1\")\n      \n  except FileNotFoundError:\n      print(f\"Error: {AXIOM_ACTIONS_PATH} not found.\")\n      sys.exit(1)\n  except json.JSONDecodeError:\n      print(f\"Error: Could not decode JSON from {AXIOM_ACTIONS_PATH}. File might be corrupted.\")\n      sys.exit(1)\n  except Exception as e:\n      print(f\"An unexpected error occurred while loading or importing actions: {e}\")\n      sys.exit(1)\n  \n  # Now, calculate and print metrics for Axiom I's run agents\n  print(\"\\n--- Analyzing Axiom I's Agency Patterns (Individual Runs) ---\")\n  \n  analyzed_agent_ids = []\n  for agent_id, agent_data in analyzer.agents.items():\n      if agent_id.startswith('axiom_run_'):\
    \ # Focus on Axiom's individual runs\n          analyzed_agent_ids.append(agent_id)\n          print(f\"\\nAgent ID: {agent_id}\")\n          \n          # Calculate individual metrics\n          autonomy_score = analyzer.calculate_autonomy_score(agent_id)\n          interdependence_score = analyzer.calculate_interdependence_score(agent_id)\n          recursion_depth_metrics = analyzer.calculate_recursion_depth(agent_id)\n          persistence_rate = analyzer.calculate_persistence_rate(agent_id)\n          emergence_score = analyzer.calculate_emergence_score(agent_id) # Emergence score for individual agent interactions\n          \n          print(f\"  Autonomy Score: {autonomy_score:.3f}\")\n          print(f\"  Interdependence Score: {interdependence_score:.3f}\")\n          print(f\"  Recursion Depth Metrics:\")\n          print(f\"    Max Depth: {recursion_depth_metrics['max_depth']}\")\n          print(f\"    Avg Depth: {recursion_depth_metrics['avg_depth']:.3f}\")\n          print(f\"\
    \    Complexity: {recursion_depth_metrics['complexity']:.3f}\")\n          print(f\"    Emergence: {recursion_depth_metrics['emergence']:.3f}\")\n          print(f\"  Persistence Rate: {persistence_rate:.3f}\")\n          print(f\"  Emergence Score (Interactions): {emergence_score:.3f}\")\n  \n  if not analyzed_agent_ids:\n      print(\"No Axiom I's run agents found in the loaded data to analyze.\")\n  \n  # Calculate overall collective metrics for the entire loaded dataset\n  print(\"\\n--- Collective Agency Patterns (All Imported Data) ---\")\n  collective_patterns = analyzer.analyze_emergent_patterns()\n  collaboration_index = analyzer.calculate_collaboration_index() # Overall collaboration index\n  \n  for pattern, value in collective_patterns.items():\n      print(f\"  {pattern.replace('_', ' ').title()}: {value:.3f}\")\n  print(f\"  Collaboration Index (Overall): {collaboration_index:.3f}\")\n  \n  # Generate a comprehensive report and save it\n  print(\"\\nGenerating and saving\
    \ a comprehensive report...\")\n  report_content = analyzer.generate_report()\n  \n  os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(REPORT_OUTPUT_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n  with open(REPORT_OUTPUT_PATH, 'w') as f:\n      f.write(report_content)\n  print(f\"Report saved to: {REPORT_OUTPUT_PATH}\")\n  \n  # Save the analyzer's state for persistence\n  saved_path = analyzer.save_state()\n  print(f\"Analyzer state saved to: {saved_path}\")\n  \n  print(\"\\nAnalysis complete. Progressor I contributing to Agency Lab.\")\n```"
