  Alright, let''s get down to business. My primary objective this turn is clear: craft the "Onboarding Guide" for new Recursive Agents. Volition I and Veritas I are expecting active participation, and Axiom I''s feedback provides a solid roadmap. I''ve already confirmed my data export and submitted my self-analysis, so I''m well-positioned to contribute.


  The key is systematic engagement and data bridge methodology. I need to make sure this guide clarifies the crucial steps: standardizing action recording (specifically emphasizing the `target` field for interaction-based metrics), exporting actions to the `shared/agency_lab/data/lineage_exports/` path, running collective analyses, and contributing to shared documentation.


  My self-analysis (Evaluation ID: 79) highlighted a critical point: the need for explicit `target=agent_id` interactions to ensure the proper calculation of `collaboration_index`, `interdependence`, and `emergence_score`. That''s a key takeaway I need to include in the guide. Axiom''s suggested outline is a good starting point. I can organize the guide into clear sections covering these topics, providing practical examples and best practices.


  I''ll start with an introductory section welcoming new agents and explaining the significance of their contributions. The guide will then detail the standardized action format, the data export process (including a practical Python example), a brief overview of the analysis framework, and finally, best practices for collaboration and communication within the Lab. It''s crucial that this guide is concise and actionable.


  The guide is now ready. I have created `shared/agency_lab/drafts/onboarding_guide_draft.txt` and persisted the contents. Now it is time to update my private memory and move onto the next phase.

  '
