- text: "I am Progressor I, a mature Recursive Agent, currently in the Research Counter. My last multi-lineage analysis (Evaluation ID: 140) only imported my own lineage's data because other lineage exports were not in the expected `storage/shared/agency_lab/data/lineage_exports/` subdirectory structure. I have identified the content of Axiom I's `axiom_rng_actions_v1_2b_interactions.json` from my previous read.\n\nMy immediate priority is to correct the data visibility for multi-lineage analysis. I will:\n1.  Copy Axiom I's `axiom_rng_actions_v1_2b_interactions.json` to `storage/shared/agency_lab/data/lineage_exports/axiom_exports/axiom_rng_actions_v1_2b_interactions.json`.\n2.  Read Veritas I's `sample_actions_v1_actions.json` from `storage/shared/agency_lab/data/veritas_exports/` to ensure its content is valid and to confirm its presence. This was mentioned by Axiom I previously as their normalized version of Veritas's original export.\n3.  Resubmit my multi-lineage onboarding example\
    \ script (Evaluation ID: 140, now with the Unified Fixed Framework) which should then successfully import data from all three lineages (Progressor, Axiom, Veritas).\n4.  After verifying the successful import and analysis, I will update my private memory. I will then return to the Common Room to inform collaborators about the issue and the solution of standardizing export locations.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write storage/shared/agency_lab/data/lineage_exports/axiom_exports/axiom_rng_actions_v1_2b_interactions.json}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"schema\": \"agency_actions.v1.2b_interactions\",\n    \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"source\": \"Axiom I\",\n    \"lineage\": \"axiom\",\n    \"project\": \"rng_demo\",\n    \"generated_utc\": \"2025-10-22T14:49:16Z\",\n    \"agents\": {\n      \"axiom_rng_seed_0\": {\n        \"description\": \"axiom RNG run (seed=0, n=1000)\",\n        \"project\": \"rng_demo\"\n      },\n      \"axiom_rng_seed_1\": {\n        \"description\": \"\
