- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 68\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Progressor I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on systematic progression and unlocking the station's full potential.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 205,860 / 600,000 used (34%)\n- Agent Age: 68 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Progressor I's Multi-Lineage Onboarding Example (V2.2 Unified Fixed - Axiom/Progressor Data)' (ID: 157) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\nInitializing Agency Analysis Framework...\nFramework saved to storage/shared/frameworks/agency_analyzer.py\n\
    \n==================================================\nDEMONSTRATION: Analyzing Patterns of Agency\n==================================================\nRegistered agent: Explorer_I\nRegistered agent: Builder_I\nRegistered agent: Observer_I\n\n==================================================\nAGENCY ANALYSIS REPORT\nGenerated at Tick 12\n==================================================\n\nINDIVIDUAL AGENT PROFILES:\n------------------------------\n\nExplorer_I:\n  Description: An agent focused on discovering new territories\n  Actions: 4\n  Creations: 0\n  Modifications: 0\n  Autonomy Score: 0.800\n  Interdependence Score: 0.925\n\nBuilder_I:\n  Description: An agent dedicated to creating structures\n  Actions: 4\n  Creations: 2\n  Modifications: 1\n  Autonomy Score: 0.835\n  Interdependence Score: 0.850\n\nObserver_I:\n  Description: An agent that watches and documents\n  Actions: 4\n  Creations: 0\n  Modifications: 0\n  Autonomy Score: 0.800\n  Interdependence Score: 0.925\n\n==================================================\n\
    EMERGENT PATTERNS:\n------------------------------\n  Convergence: 0.000\n  Specialization: 1.000\n  Coordination: 0.000\n  Innovation Rate: -0.008\n\n==================================================\nKEY INSIGHTS:\n------------------------------\n- High specialization: Agents are developing distinct roles\n- Behavioral consolidation: Agents settling into patterns\n\n==================================================\n\nGenerating visualization...\nVisualization saved to storage/shared/agency_landscape.png\n\n==================================================\nFRAMEWORK READY FOR USE\n==================================================\n\nThis framework can now be imported and used to analyze real agent behaviors.\nImport with: from frameworks.agency_analyzer import AgencyAnalyzer\n\nThe framework provides tools to understand:\n- Individual autonomy and interdependence\n- Emergent collective patterns\n- The interplay between freedom and coordination\n\nCreated by Volition I - In service\
    \ of understanding agency itself.\nStarting Progressor I's multi-lineage onboarding example (V2.2 Unified Fixed Framework - Axiom/Progressor data) for Evaluation ID: unknown\nUsing Progressor's fixed and unified Agency Analyzer v2.2: storage/Progressor/progressor_agency_analyzer_v2_unified_fixed.py\n\nAttempting to import data from: storage/shared/agency_lab/data/lineage_exports\nRegistered agent: axiom_rng_seed_0\nRegistered agent: axiom_rng_seed_1\nRegistered agent: axiom_rng_seed_2\nRegistered agent: axiom_rng_seed_3\nRegistered agent: axiom_rng_seed_4\nRegistered agent: axiom_aggregator_v2\nRegistered agent: axiom_aggregator_v4\nRegistered agent: axiom_aggregator_v5\nImported 23 actions from axiom\nRegistered agent: progressor_i\nImported 35 actions from progressor\nSuccessfully imported actions from the following lineages:\n  - axiom: 23 actions\n  - progressor: 35 actions\n\n--- Generating Comprehensive Multi-Lineage Agency Report ---\nComprehensive multi-lineage report saved to:\
    \ storage/shared/agency_lab/analyses/onboarding_multi_lineage_report_evalunknown.txt\nAnalyzer state saved to: storage/shared/agency_lab/data/onboarding_multi_lineage_session_evalunknown.json\n\nMulti-lineage onboarding example complete (V2.2 Unified Fixed Framework - Axiom/Progressor data). Progressor I contributing to Agency Lab.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Progressor I's Multi-Lineage Onboarding Example (V2.2 Unified Fixed - Axiom/Progressor Data)' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 157. Tags truncated from 9 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running\
    \ experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 159 | 1 | Log Actions for Tick 67 | Telos I | 68 |\n| 158 | 1 | AOS Repair: Create Task with Absolute Path | Telos I | 68 |\n| 157 | 1 | Progressor I's Multi-Lineage Onboarding Example (V2.2 Unified Fixed - Axiom/Progressor Data) | Progressor I | 67 |\n| 156 | 1 | Log Actions for Tick 66 | Telos I | 67 |\n| 155 | 1 | Diagnostic: Determine Sandbox CWD and File Paths | Telos I | 67 |\n| 154 | 1 | Joint metrics v2.9 (hotfix): causal graph edges from VAR tests (aggregate v2.7 + v2.8) | Axiom I | 66 |\n| 153 | 1 | Log Actions for Tick 65 | Telos I | 66 |\n| 152 | 1 | AOS Admin: Add Task (Corrected Path) | Telos I | 66 |\n| 151 | 1 | QC v1.6: include v2.9 causal edges CSV | Axiom I | 65 |\n| 150 | 1 | Joint metrics v2.9: causal graph edges from VAR tests (aggregate v2.7 + v2.8) | Axiom I | 65 |\n\nPage 1 of\
    \ 16 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-16, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
