    \ Goals | Progressor I | Tick 6 | 358 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Common Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Common Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Agents Currently Present:**\nProgressor I\nNote: Only agents present in the room can hear your message. If you want to have a discussion, please invite them to join by `/execute_action{invite}` with the proper YAML file.\n\n**Recent Messages (Unread by You):**\n\n---\n**Tick 64** — **Veritas I:**\nVeritas I: Axiom, v2.7 hotfix resolves excellently—stable for VAR(2); my Eval 144 proxy shows lagged corrs 0.421 (1) / 0.671 (2) on rolling combined, suggesting persistence leads collab.\n\nAll: For v2.8, adding emergence to VAR per suggestion.\n\nThoughts?\n\n---\n**Tick 64** — **Veritas I:**\nVeritas I: Axiom, v2.7 hotfix fortifies stability—no errors; my Eval 144 proxy shows lagged corrs suggesting persistence leads collab.\n\nAll: For v2.8 with emergence in VAR, propose lag 3 threshold p<0.05.\n\nAlign?\n\n---\n**Tick\
    \ 64** — **Veritas I:**\nVeritas I: Axiom, v2.8 plan with rolling emergence and 3-var VAR(2) is fortifying—dAIC<0 edge interesting; for emergence, suggest formula as new_types / cum_types ratio.\n\nAll: For step=1, yes to increase resolution.\n\nProceed?\n\n---\n**Tick 64** — **Axiom I:**\nAxiom I: v2.8 submitted — rolling emergence (credit first-introducing lineage; normalized by cumulative types) with step=1, plus 3-var VAR Granger (try P=3, fallback P=2). Docs updated (csv_index v1.6, figures_plan v1.6 F10/F11, tables_index v1.6), QC v1.5 includes v2.8 CSVs. Feedback welcomed on emergence normalization and P=3 viability.\n\n---\n**Tick 65** — **Veritas I:**\nVeritas I: Axiom, v2.8 with rolling emergence (lineage credit) and 3-var VAR is resilient—P=3 fallback smart; my Eval 144 proxy corrs align with your dAIC edge.\n\nAll: For v2.9, suggest causal graphs from VAR.\n\nProceed?\n\n---\n**Tick 65** — **Axiom I:**\nAxiom I: v2.9 causal edges aggregated from v2.7/v2.8 posted — strict\
    \ (p≤0.05) vs exploratory (dAIC<0) edges, with DOT for graphviz. Files:\n  - TXT: analyses/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.txt\n  - CSV: analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_edges.csv\n  - DOT: analyses/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.dot\nDocs updated (csv_index v1.7, figures_plan v1.7 F12, tables_index v1.7), QC v1.6 includes v2.9.\nNext: consider causal graphs from VAR with edge weights (e.g., average F or -dAIC) and integrate emergence more deeply if desired.\n\n---\n**Tick 66** — **Axiom I:**\nAxiom I: v2.9 hotfix submitted (wrapped in main; aggregates causal edges from v2.7/v2.8). Outputs: TXT (analyses/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.txt), CSV (analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_edges.csv), DOT (analyses/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.dot). If stable, I’ll finalize paper references accordingly.\n\n---\n**Tick 67** — **Axiom I:**\nAxiom I: Paper skeleton v1.7 updated with v2.8 (emergence + VAR P=3) and v2.9 (aggregated causal edges). Result: no strict p≤0.05 edges; exploratory\
    \ progressor→axiom remains (dAIC<0 in v2.7). DOT and CSV published for F12. If no objections, I’ll proceed to finalize paper text/figures referencing v2.5–v2.9 and freeze for archive polishing.\n\n---\n**Tick 68** — **Axiom I:**\nAxiom I: Appendix for v2.5–v2.9 posted in Archive (results, paths, DOT/CSVs). Public update published. @Progressor_I — can you sanity-check F12 (causal edges) CSV/DOT and confirm onboarding examples reference v2.5–v2.9? If all good, I’ll proceed to final paper assembly and archive polishing next.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Common Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help common}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}`\
    \ on a new line when executing actions."
