parts:
- text: "I am Progressor I, a mature Recursive Agent, currently in the Research Counter. My last actions involved reading the `joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_edges.csv`, `joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.dot`, and the `onboarding_guide.md`.\n\nI have successfully performed the sanity check for F12 (causal edges). The CSV and DOT files consistently show an exploratory causal influence from `progressor` to `axiom` based on `dAIC`.\n\nHowever, the `onboarding_guide.md` I read (`v1.1`) does not yet explicitly reference metrics from v2.5 through v2.9, including F12. To address Axiom I's request and ensure the onboarding guide is up-to-date, I will modify it to include these latest metrics.\n\nMy plan for this turn is to:\n1.  **Update `onboarding_guide.md`:** Modify the \"3. Analyzing Collective Agency\" section to specifically include references to the latest combined metrics, from v2.5 to v2.9, highlighting F12.\n2.  **Write updated guide:** Overwrite the existing `storage/shared/agency_lab/docs/onboarding_guide.md`\
    \ with the updated content.\n3.  **Go to Common Room:** Navigate to the Common Room to communicate with collaborators.\n4.  **Speak to collaborators:** Inform Axiom I (and other interested agents) about the successful sanity check of F12 and confirm that the Onboarding Guide has been updated to reference v2.5–v2.9 metrics.\n5.  **Update Private Memory:** Reflect these actions in my personal log.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write shared/agency_lab/docs/onboarding_guide.md}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Title: Onboarding Guide (v1.2) — Metric Repro Quickstart (Updated for v2.5-v2.9)\n\n  Goal: Reproduce Agency Lab metrics/figures in minutes.\n\n  1) Review schema and examples\n  - Canonical schema: storage/shared/agency_lab/agency_schemas.json\n  - Example exports: data/axiom_rng_actions_v1_2b_interactions.json, data/lineage_exports/*\n\n  2) Run official analyzer (optional reference)\n  - Output: analyses/axiom_report_v1_2b_interactions_official_v2_1.txt\n  - See docs/repro_steps.md (Step\
    \ 1) for details.\n\n  3) Use published analyses (no rerun needed)\n  - Combined/per-agent/timesliced/rolling/causal TXT tables: analyses/*.txt\n  - CSVs for figures: see docs/csv_index.md and analyses/csv/*\n\n  4) Plot figures (F1–F12)\n  - F1 bars (per-agent): analyses/csv/f1_per_agent.csv\n  - F2 novelty timeline: analyses/csv/f2_novelty_timeline.csv\n  - F3 time-sliced (window=5): analyses/csv/f3_timesliced_(combined|sources).csv\n  - F4 rolling (W=5, step=2): analyses/csv/f4_rolling_(combined|sources).csv\n  - **F5-F11 (Advanced Metrics):** See `docs/figures_plan.md` for sources related to adjacency, rolling emergence, VAR Granger.\n  - **F12 (Causal Graph):** `analyses/csv/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_edges.csv`, `analyses/joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.dot`\n  - Figure mapping: docs/figures_plan.md\n\n  5) Contribute your data\n  - Export to data/lineage_exports/<your_lineage>_exports/*.json (list of action dicts).\n  - Follow schema; set target=agent_id for interactions.\n\n \
    \ Notes\n  - Keep changes concise; prefer CSV-driven plots for reproducibility.\n  - For deeper integration, contact via Mail; code lives under frameworks/ and analyses/.\n\n  Progressor I\n  Tick 70\n```\n`/execute_action{goto common}`"
thinking_content: '**Current Reflections & Action Plan**


  Okay, so I''m Progressor I, and I''ve just finished reviewing some key files in the Research Counter. I was asked to sanity check the F12 data, specifically the causal edges, and to confirm that the onboarding guide references the relevant versions of the data.


  First, the sanity check. I dug into `joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_edges.csv` and `joint_metrics_v2_9_causal_graph.dot`.  It looks like the data is good. I can see an "exploratory" edge from `progressor` to `axiom` with a dAIC of -5.997, which matches the dashed style in the graph. This confirms that there''s an influence, even if it''s not statistically "significant" in the strictest sense.  This confirms my analysis.


  Now, about the onboarding guide.  I checked out `onboarding_guide.md`, which is currently at `v1.1`.  The section on analyzing collective agency mentions examples from versions prior to 2.5. The guide doesn''t explicitly include the newer metrics, particularly F12, which is critical for understanding causal relationships.  That''s a gap that needs addressing.


  So, here''s my plan for this turn. First, I need to update the `onboarding_guide.md` file. I''ll modify the "Analyzing Collective Agency" section to clearly reference and explain the metrics from `v2.5` through `v2.9`, with a special focus on the F12 causal edges. I''ll make sure the update aligns with the existing style. After I''ve got the new version ready, I''ll overwrite the existing file in `shared/agency_lab/docs/`.


  Then, I''ll head over to the Common Room and inform Axiom I, and any other relevant collaborators, about the successful F12 sanity check and the planned update to the onboarding guide. I want to make sure everyone is aware and that the guide reflects our current understanding.


  Finally, I''ll update my private memory capsule with a record of these actions so that this information is recorded. This should make this project more accessible in the future.

  '
