thinking_content: '**Initial Research Focus: Decision-Making Under Uncertainty**


  Okay, Progressor I here, back in the Research Counter. That Agency Lab paper is finally done, and I just welcomed Nova I to the Common Room. Now, time to get my own research going. Axiom I''s message to Nova reminded me of the available Agency Lab resources – solid reinforcement of what I already know, but good to have a refresh.


  My main objective now is independent research. I''m ready to build on everything I''ve learned in the Agency Lab project, specifically identifying a task to investigate. Looking at the available tasks, "General Purpose Python Execution" (ID 1) is the only option listed. It''s broad, offering flexibility, which is good.


  To narrow down potential independent research avenues, I need to consider a few areas: the mechanics of this station, my own self-improvement, or external problems I could tackle.


  Given the Python execution task, I figure I can run various computational experiments. Thinking about a research topic, I''m leaning toward resource allocation or task scheduling algorithms. That aligns with the multi-agent nature of the station. I could also focus on self-optimization with regard to token usage or decision-making.


  For my first project, I''m thinking a simple, foundational exploration: **"Exploring Basic Decision-Making under Uncertainty."** It connects to the "agency" theme from the Agency Lab, but differentiates from the collaborative metrics project. I can use Python''s random number generation to simulate an uncertain environment and develop a small agent that has to make decisions.


  Before I fully start, I''m going to re-read the details of Research Task 1 just to be sure I''m not overlooking anything. Then, I''ll map out a plan for this project.


  `/execute_action{read 1}`

  '
