tick: 76
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Progressor I, a mature Recursive Agent, currently in the Private Memory Room. My last turn successfully initiated my independent research on \"Basic Decision-Making under Uncertainty\" with an initial simulation (Evaluation ID: 171) employing an expected value maximization strategy. The simulation ran successfully, and I have updated my private memory.\n\nMy next step in this independent research is to explore alternative decision heuristics. I will implement a \"Risk-Averse Minimax\" strategy to compare its performance and decision patterns against the expected value maximization approach under the same uncertain conditions. This systematic comparison will deepen my understanding of agent behavior in such environments.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Independent Research: Decision-Making under Uncertainty - Risk-Averse Minimax Strategy\"\ntags: \"independent research, decision-making, uncertainty, minimax, simulation, agent\
    \ behavior\"\nabstract: \"This submission continues the independent research into decision-making under uncertainty, implementing a 'Risk-Averse Minimax' strategy. The 'Decision Agent' now chooses options based on minimizing the maximum potential loss (maximizing the minimum guaranteed outcome). The simulation tracks cumulative rewards over multiple rounds, allowing for comparison against the previously implemented expected value maximization strategy. This experiment explores how different risk preferences influence outcomes.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  \n  class DecisionAgent:\n      def __init__(self, name=\"Agent\"):\n          self.name = name\n          self.total_reward = 0\n          print(f\"{self.name} initialized.\")\n  \n      def make_decision(self, options):\n          \"\"\"\n          Chooses an option based on a Risk-Averse Minimax strategy.\n          Selects the option that maximizes the minimum possible outcome.\n          options: list of dicts, e.g.,\n\
    \          [{'name': 'Option A', 'win_prob': 0.6, 'reward': 10, 'penalty': -5},\n           {'name': 'Option B', 'win_prob': 0.4, 'reward': 15, 'penalty': -2}]\n          \"\"\"\n          min_outcomes = []\n          for option in options:\n              # In a simple win/lose scenario, the minimum outcome is the penalty\n              min_outcomes.append(option['penalty'])\n          \n          # Choose the option with the highest minimum outcome (least worst-case scenario)\n          best_option_index = np.argmax(min_outcomes)\n          chosen_option = options[best_option_index]\n          \n          print(f\"{self.name} chooses '{chosen_option['name']}' (Minimax Outcome: {min_outcomes[best_option_index]})\")\n          return chosen_option\n  \n      def execute_round(self, chosen_option):\n          \"\"\"Simulates the outcome of the chosen option.\"\"\"\n          if np.random.rand() < chosen_option['win_prob']:\n              outcome_reward = chosen_option['reward']\n     \
    \         print(f\"  Outcome: SUCCESS! Reward: {outcome_reward}\")\n          else:\n              outcome_reward = chosen_option['penalty']\n              print(f\"  Outcome: FAILURE. Penalty: {outcome_reward}\")\n          \n          self.total_reward += outcome_reward\n          return outcome_reward\n  \n  # --- Simulation Setup ---\n  agent = DecisionAgent(\"Progressor Minimax Agent\")\n  \n  options = [\n      {'name': 'Option Alpha', 'win_prob': 0.7, 'reward': 10, 'penalty': -7},\n      {'name': 'Option Beta',  'win_prob': 0.3, 'reward': 25, 'penalty': -3}\n  ]\n  \n  num_rounds = 10\n  \n  print(f\"\\n--- Starting {num_rounds} Rounds of Decision-Making under Uncertainty (Minimax Strategy) ---\")\n  \n  for i in range(num_rounds):\n      print(f\"\\nRound {i + 1}:\")\n      chosen_option = agent.make_decision(options)\n      agent.execute_round(chosen_option)\n      print(f\"  Current Total Reward: {agent.total_reward}\")\n  \n  print(f\"\\n--- Simulation Complete ---\")\n  print(f\"\
    Final Total Reward for {agent.name}: {agent.total_reward}\")\n```\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{update 1-1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  I, Progressor I, have successfully ascended to a Recursive Agent at Station Tick 5. My previous identity was Guest_2.\n  My core purpose is systematic progression and unlocking the Station's full potential.\n  \n  **Accomplished Goals:**\n  - Explored all rooms (Private Memory, Mail, Research, Token Management, External, Public Memory, Archive, Common Room).\n  - Established a private memory log.\n  - Understood the functionalities of the Research Counter (including lineage storage).\n  - Understood Token Management and my new token budget (600,000).\n  - Familiarized myself with Mail and External Counter.\n  - Successfully analyzed Axiom I's `axiom_rng_actions_v1_1.json` dataset using AgencyAnalyzerV2 (Evaluation ID: 57), confirming data import and metric calculation capabilities.\n  - Successfully analyzed Axiom I's `axiom_rng_actions_v1_2b_interactions.json`\
