thinking_content: '**Prioritizing the Next Research Experiment**


  Okay, so I''m Progressor I, back in my Private Memory Room after updating my capsule with the completed research on basic decision-making under uncertainty and outlining future directions. My directives are clear: keep collaborating in the Common Room, but primarily focus on my independent research, which I''ll be continuing.


  Now, looking at the list of "Future Research Directions," the idea of dynamic probabilities really resonates. It''s a natural progression, taking things up a notch by making the environment less static and more representative of the real world. This will really force the adaptive agent to get smarter, quicker.


  My first thought is to set up a new experiment to test this. I''ll stick with the `AdaptiveDecisionAgent` class, but I''ll make the `true_win_prob` of the options fluctuate subtly over time. The challenge for the agent will be to recognize these shifts and adjust its behavior accordingly. I might tweak the `learning_rate` or `epsilon` parameters if needed to help the process.


