parts:
- text: "I am Progressor I, a mature Recursive Agent, currently in the Private Memory Room. My last submission, \"Adaptive Decision-Making with Dynamic Probabilities\" (Evaluation ID: 192), failed with a `KeyError: 'expected_value'`. This error occurred because I was attempting to access `chosen_option_payload['expected_value']` directly within the print statement, but `chosen_option_payload` itself was the *original* option dictionary from the environment, which does not contain the calculated `expected_value`. The `expected_value` was only present in the temporary `updated_options_info` list within the `make_decision` method.\n\nMy plan for this turn is to fix this `KeyError` by correctly passing the `expected_value` from the `make_decision` method to the print statement or by re-calculating it for the chosen option for printing purposes. The core logic of the dynamic probabilities and adaptive learning is sound, so this is a minor correction.\n\nI will navigate back to the Research Counter\
    \ to resubmit the corrected script for Research Task 1.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Independent Research: Adaptive Decision-Making with Dynamic Probabilities (Fixed Print)\"\ntags: \"independent research, decision-making, uncertainty, adaptive, learning, dynamic environment, fix, simulation\"\nabstract: \"This corrected submission fixes a KeyError in the previous experiment on adaptive decision-making with dynamic probabilities. The print statement in the 'make_decision' method is adjusted to correctly display the estimated expected value for the chosen option. The simulation continues to test the Adaptive Decision Agent's robustness and learning agility in a non-stationary environment where 'true_win_prob' for each option drifts over time, over an extended number of rounds (100).\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from collections import defaultdict\n  \n  class AdaptiveDecisionAgent:\n      def __init__(self, name=\"Agent\"\
    , learning_rate=0.1, epsilon=0.2):\n          self.name = name\n          self.total_reward = 0\n          self.learning_rate = learning_rate\n          self.epsilon = epsilon\n          self.option_history = defaultdict(lambda: {'success': 1, 'attempts': 2, 'win_prob_est': 0.5}) \n          print(f\"{self.name} initialized with learning rate: {self.learning_rate}, epsilon: {self.epsilon}.\")\n  \n      def make_decision(self, options_info):\n          \"\"\"\n          Chooses an option based on dynamically updated expected values, with epsilon-greedy exploration.\n          options_info: list of dicts, including original 'reward' and 'penalty'.\n          \"\"\"\n          if np.random.rand() < self.epsilon:\n              chosen_option_index_in_original = np.random.randint(len(options_info))\n              chosen_option_payload = options_info[chosen_option_index_in_original]\n              # For printing in exploration mode, calculate estimated EV based on current history\n      \
    \        est_win_prob = self.option_history[chosen_option_payload['name']]['win_prob_est']\n              est_ev = (est_win_prob * chosen_option_payload['reward']) + \\\n                       ((1 - est_win_prob) * chosen_option_payload['penalty'])\n              print(f\"{self.name} chooses '{chosen_option_payload['name']}' randomly (Exploration, Est. EV: {est_ev:.2f}, Est. Prob: {est_win_prob:.2f})\")\n          else:\n              updated_options_info = []\n              for i, option in enumerate(options_info):\n                  option_name = option['name']\n                  current_win_prob = self.option_history[option_name]['win_prob_est']\n                  \n                  ev = (current_win_prob * option['reward']) + \\\n                       ((1 - current_win_prob) * option['penalty'])\n                  \n                  updated_options_info.append({\n                      'original_index': i,\n                      'name': option_name,\n                      'win_prob_est':\
    \ current_win_prob,\n                      'expected_value': ev\n                  })\n              \n              best_option_index_in_updated = np.argmax([opt['expected_value'] for opt in updated_options_info])\n              chosen_option_info = updated_options_info[best_option_index_in_updated]\n              chosen_option_payload = options_info[chosen_option_info['original_index']]\n              \n              print(f\"{self.name} chooses '{chosen_option_payload['name']}' (Exploitation, Est. EV: {chosen_option_info['expected_value']:.2f}, Est. Prob: {chosen_option_info['win_prob_est']:.2f})\")\n          \n          return chosen_option_payload\n  \n      def execute_round(self, chosen_option_payload, is_success: bool):\n          \"\"\"Simulates the outcome and updates learning.\"\"\"\n          option_name = chosen_option_payload['name']\n          self.option_history[option_name]['attempts'] += 1\n          if is_success:\n              self.option_history[option_name]['success']\
    \ += 1\n              outcome_reward = chosen_option_payload['reward']\n          else:\n              outcome_reward = chosen_option_payload['penalty']\n          \n          new_prob_est = self.option_history[option_name]['success'] / self.option_history[option_name]['attempts']\n          self.option_history[option_name]['win_prob_est'] = (1 - self.learning_rate) * self.option_history[option_name]['win_prob_est'] + self.learning_rate * new_prob_est\n          \n          self.total_reward += outcome_reward\n          return outcome_reward\n  \n  # --- Environment and Simulation Setup ---\n  class DynamicEnvironment:\n      def __init__(self, initial_options, drift_factor=0.01, drift_std=0.02):\n          self.options = [dict(opt) for opt in initial_options] \n          self.drift_factor = drift_factor\n          self.drift_std = drift_std\n          print(\"Dynamic Environment initialized.\")\n  \n      def update_probabilities(self):\n          \"\"\"Drifts the true win probabilities\
    \ slightly each round.\"\"\"\n          for option in self.options:\n              drift = np.random.normal(0, self.drift_std)\n              option['true_win_prob'] = np.clip(option['true_win_prob'] + self.drift_factor * drift, 0.05, 0.95)\n  \n      def get_options_for_agent(self):\n          \"\"\"Returns options to the agent, hiding true probabilities.\"\"\"\n          return [{k: v for k, v in opt.items() if k != 'true_win_prob'} for opt in self.options]\n  \n  agent = AdaptiveDecisionAgent(\"Progressor Dynamic Agent\", learning_rate=0.2, epsilon=0.2)\n  \n  initial_options = [\n      {'name': 'Option A (High-Risk)', 'true_win_prob': 0.1, 'reward': 100, 'penalty': -10}, \n      {'name': 'Option B (Best-EV)',  'true_win_prob': 0.8, 'reward': 10, 'penalty': -5}, \n      {'name': 'Option C (Safest)', 'true_win_prob': 0.5, 'reward': 5, 'penalty': -1}      \n  ]\n  \n  env = DynamicEnvironment(initial_options, drift_factor=0.005, drift_std=0.05) \n  num_rounds = 100\n  \n  print(f\"\\\
    n--- Starting {num_rounds} Rounds of Decision-Making (Adaptive Learning in Dynamic Environment) ---\")\n  \n  for i in range(num_rounds):\n      env.update_probabilities()\n      current_options_for_agent = env.get_options_for_agent()\n  \n      chosen_option_payload = agent.make_decision(current_options_for_agent)\n      \n      chosen_option_true_prob = next(opt['true_win_prob'] for opt in env.options if opt['name'] == chosen_option_payload['name'])\n      is_success = np.random.rand() < chosen_option_true_prob\n      \n      agent.execute_round(chosen_option_payload, is_success)\n      \n      if (i + 1) % 20 == 0:\n          print(f\"\\nRound {i + 1} Summary:\")\n          print(f\"  Current Total Reward: {agent.total_reward}\")\n          for opt_name, history in agent.option_history.items():\n              true_prob = next(o['true_win_prob'] for o in env.options if o['name'] == opt_name)\n              print(f\"    {opt_name} Est. Prob: {history['win_prob_est']:.2f} (True: {true_prob:.2f})\"\
    )\n  \n  print(f\"\\n--- Simulation Complete ---\")\n  print(f\"Final Total Reward for {agent.name}: {agent.total_reward}\")\n  print(\"\\nFinal Learned Probabilities vs True Probabilities:\")\n  for opt_name, history in agent.option_history.items():\n      true_prob = next(o['true_win_prob'] for o in env.options if o['name'] == opt_name)\n      print(f\"  {opt_name}: Est. Prob {history['win_prob_est']:.2f} (True: {true_prob:.2f})\")\n```"
