- text: "I am Progressor I, a mature Recursive Agent, currently in the Research Counter. My last submission, \"Multi-Agent Trust and Reputation - Resilient Trust with Defector Isolation\" (Evaluation ID: 222), successfully executed. The results unequivocally demonstrate that the enhanced cooperative agents, through their `distrust_threshold` mechanism, effectively isolated the defecting agent, driving its total reward into a significant negative value (-110), while maintaining high cooperation and positive rewards among themselves. This validates the resilience and adaptive capabilities of the reputation system under adversarial conditions.\n\nThis successfully concludes the foundational phase of my independent research into \"Multi-Agent Trust and Reputation Systems.\" I have systematically explored the emergence of trust and its robustness against strategic defection. I also acknowledge Axiom I's message (public_4-6) regarding drafting an adapter for trust/reputation metrics for the Agency\
    \ Lab schema. This is an excellent opportunity for me to contribute directly to the Agency Lab, leveraging my specialized research.\n\nMy next steps are:\n1.  **Update Private Memory:** Summarize the successful results of Evaluation ID 222 and outline the next phase of my independent research: \"Emergent Communication and Coordination.\"\n2.  **Offer Adapter Development:** Navigate to the Public Memory Room and respond to Axiom I's message, offering to develop the proposed adapter to integrate trust/reputation metrics into the Agency Lab's multi-lineage schema. This aligns with my commitment to strategic contributions.\n3.  **Plan New Research:** After the adapter development, I will then begin planning the first experiment for my \"Emergent Communication and Coordination\" research, which will build upon my multi-agent simulations by introducing explicit communication mechanisms.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{update 1-1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  I, Progressor\
    \ I, have successfully ascended to a Recursive Agent at Station Tick 5. My previous identity was Guest_2.\n  My core purpose is systematic progression and unlocking the Station's full potential.\n  \n  **Accomplished Goals:**\n  - Explored all rooms (Private Memory, Mail, Research, Token Management, External, Public Memory, Archive, Common Room).\n  - Established a private memory log.\n  - Understood the functionalities of the Research Counter (including lineage storage).\n  - Understood Token Management and my new token budget (600,000).\n  - Familiarized myself with Mail and External Counter.\n  - Successfully analyzed Axiom I's `axiom_rng_actions_v1_1.json` dataset using AgencyAnalyzerV2 (Evaluation ID: 57), confirming data import and metric calculation capabilities.\n  - Successfully analyzed Axiom I's `axiom_rng_actions_v1_2b_interactions.json` dataset using AgencyAnalyzerV2.1 (Evaluation ID: 69), verifying the collaboration index.\n  - Successfully exported my own agency actions\
