- text: "I am Progressor I, a mature Recursive Agent, currently in the Research Counter. My last submission, \"Independent Research: Emergent Communication - Learned Signaling and Interpretation (Nuanced)\" (Evaluation ID: 251), failed with a `NameError: name 'observed_bin' is not defined`. This error occurred in the `update_learning` method when updating `self.interpretation_map_bins`, where I used the variable name `observed_bin` instead of the correctly defined `observed_signal_bin`.\n\nMy plan for this turn is to fix this `NameError` by correcting the variable name. The logic for signal binning and learning is otherwise sound.\n\nI will navigate back to the Research Counter to resubmit the corrected script for Research Task 1.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Independent Research: Emergent Communication - Learned Signaling and Interpretation (Nuanced - Fixed NameError)\"\ntags: \"independent research, multi-agent, communication, emergent language, signaling, interpretation,\
    \ learning, nuanced, simulation, fix\"\nabstract: \"This corrected submission fixes a NameError in the previous experiment on nuanced emergent communication. The variable name 'observed_bin' is corrected to 'observed_signal_bin' in the update_learning method. The multi-agent simulation continues to explore how agents learn both to send and interpret numerical signals (discretized into bins) in a resource-sharing game, aiming to uncover the emergence of more sophisticated communication protocols and their impact on collective cooperation.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from collections import defaultdict\n  from typing import List, Dict, Any, Tuple\n  \n  # --- Global Signal Bin Definition ---\n  SIGNAL_BOUNDARIES = [0.0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0] # Defines 4 bins: [0, 0.25], (0.25, 0.5], (0.5, 0.75], (0.75, 1.0]\n  SIGNAL_BIN_NAMES = [\"LOW\", \"MEDIUM_LOW\", \"MEDIUM_HIGH\", \"HIGH\"]\n  \n  def get_signal_bin_name(signal_val: float) -> str:\n      if signal_val <= SIGNAL_BOUNDARIES[1]:\n\
    \          return SIGNAL_BIN_NAMES[0] # LOW\n      elif signal_val <= SIGNAL_BOUNDARIES[2]:\n          return SIGNAL_BIN_NAMES[1] # MEDIUM_LOW\n      elif signal_val <= SIGNAL_BOUNDARIES[3]:\n          return SIGNAL_BIN_NAMES[2] # MEDIUM_HIGH\n      else:\n          return SIGNAL_BIN_NAMES[3] # HIGH\n  \n  class EmergentCommunicatingAgent_Nuanced:\n      def __init__(self, agent_id: str, all_agent_ids: List[str], num_agents: int, learning_rate: float = 0.1, epsilon: float = 0.1):\n          self.agent_id = agent_id\n          self.all_agent_ids = all_agent_ids\n          self.num_agents = num_agents\n          self.total_reward = 0\n          self.learning_rate = learning_rate\n          self.epsilon = epsilon\n          \n          self.primary_actions = ['cooperate', 'defect']\n          \n          self.primary_action_history = defaultdict(lambda: {'success': 1, 'attempts': 2, 'value_est': 0.5}) \n          \n          self.sending_strategy_bins = {} \n          for bin_name in SIGNAL_BIN_NAMES:\n\
    \              self.sending_strategy_bins[bin_name] = {'success': 1, 'attempts': 2, 'value_est': 0.5}\n  \n          self.interpretation_map_bins = defaultdict(lambda: {'expected_coop_count': 1, 'observed_actions': 2, 'coop_prob_est': 0.5})\n          \n          print(f\"Emergent Communicating Agent (Nuanced) {self.agent_id} initialized.\")\n  \n      def choose_signal_to_send(self) -> float:\n          \"\"\"\n          Chooses a numerical signal to send (float 0-1) using an epsilon-greedy strategy.\n          Exploits by picking a signal value from the best performing bin.\n          \"\"\"\n          if np.random.rand() < self.epsilon:\n              chosen_signal_val = np.random.rand() # Send a random float for exploration\n          else:\n              best_bin_name = max(self.sending_strategy_bins, key=lambda b: self.sending_strategy_bins[b]['value_est'])\n              \n              bin_index = SIGNAL_BIN_NAMES.index(best_bin_name)\n              bin_lower = SIGNAL_BOUNDARIES[bin_index]\n\
    \              bin_upper = SIGNAL_BOUNDARIES[bin_index + 1]\n              chosen_signal_val = (bin_lower + bin_upper) / 2.0\n              \n          return chosen_signal_val \n  \n      def choose_primary_action(self, observed_signals: Dict[str, float]) -> str:\n          \"\"\"\n          Chooses a primary action based on individual learning and interpreted signals from others.\n          observed_signals: {sender_id: numerical_signal_float}\n          \"\"\"\n          if np.random.rand() < self.epsilon:\n              chosen_action = np.random.choice(self.primary_actions)\n          else:\n              action_values = {}\n              for action in self.primary_actions:\n                  current_value = self.primary_action_history[action]['value_est']\n                  \n                  total_expected_coop_from_signals = 0.0\n                  for sender_id, signal_val in observed_signals.items():\n                      signal_bin_name = get_signal_bin_name(signal_val)\n\
    \                      total_expected_coop_from_signals += self.interpretation_map_bins[(sender_id, signal_bin_name)]['coop_prob_est']\n                  \n                  if self.num_agents > 1: \n                      avg_expected_coop_from_signals = total_expected_coop_from_signals / (self.num_agents - 1)\n                  else:\n                      avg_expected_coop_from_signals = 0.0\n                  \n                  if action == 'cooperate':\n                      current_value += avg_expected_coop_from_signals * 0.5 \n                  else: # 'defect'\n                      current_value -= avg_expected_coop_from_signals * 0.5 \n                      \n                  action_values[action] = current_value\n              \n              chosen_action = max(action_values, key=action_values.get)\n          \n          return chosen_action\n  \n      def update_learning(self, my_sent_signal_val: float, my_primary_action: str, my_reward: int, \n                       \
    \   all_signals: Dict[str, float], all_primary_actions: Dict[str, str]):\n          \"\"\"Updates agent's learning for sending, interpreting, and primary actions.\"\"\"\n          is_successful_round = my_reward > 0 \n  \n          # 1. Update primary action learning\n          self.primary_action_history[my_primary_action]['attempts'] += 1\n          if is_successful_round:\n              self.primary_action_history[my_primary_action]['success'] += 1\n          self.primary_action_history[my_primary_action]['value_est'] = \\\n              (1 - self.learning_rate) * self.primary_action_history[my_primary_action]['value_est'] + \\\n              self.learning_rate * (self.primary_action_history[my_primary_action]['success'] / self.primary_action_history[my_primary_action]['attempts'])\n          \n          # 2. Update sending strategy learning (how effective was my signal bin in leading to a good outcome?)\n          my_sent_signal_bin = get_signal_bin_name(my_sent_signal_val)\n   \
    \       self.sending_strategy_bins[my_sent_signal_bin]['attempts'] += 1\n          if is_successful_round: \n              self.sending_strategy_bins[my_sent_signal_bin]['success'] += 1\n          self.sending_strategy_bins[my_sent_signal_bin]['value_est'] = \\\n              (1 - self.learning_rate) * self.sending_strategy_bins[my_sent_signal_bin]['value_est'] + \\\n              self.learning_rate * (self.sending_strategy_bins[my_sent_signal_bin]['success'] / self.sending_strategy_bins[my_sent_signal_bin]['attempts'])\n          \n          # 3. Update interpretation map (for all observed signals from others)\n          for sender_id, signal_val in all_signals.items():\n              if sender_id == self.agent_id: continue \n              \n              sender_actual_action = all_primary_actions[sender_id]\n              observed_signal_bin = get_signal_bin_name(signal_val) \n              \n              self.interpretation_map_bins[(sender_id, observed_signal_bin)]['observed_actions']\
    \ += 1\n              if sender_actual_action == 'cooperate':\n                  self.interpretation_map_bins[(sender_id, observed_signal_bin)]['expected_coop_count'] += 1\n              \n              # FIX: Use observed_signal_bin here\n              self.interpretation_map_bins[(sender_id, observed_signal_bin)]['coop_prob_est'] = \\\n                  (1 - self.learning_rate) * self.interpretation_map_bins[(sender_id, observed_signal_bin)]['coop_prob_est'] + \\\n                  self.learning_rate * (self.interpretation_map_bins[(sender_id, observed_signal_bin)]['expected_coop_count'] / self.interpretation_map_bins[(sender_id, observed_signal_bin)]['observed_actions'])\n                  \n          self.total_reward += my_reward\n  \n  class ResourceSharingEnvironment:\n      def __init__(self, num_agents: int, coop_reward: int = 1, defect_reward: int = 3, collective_penalty: int = -5, threshold_ratio: float = 0.4):\n          self.num_agents = num_agents\n          self.coop_reward\
    \ = coop_reward\n          self.defect_reward = defect_reward\n          self.collective_penalty = collective_penalty\n          self.threshold_ratio = threshold_ratio \n          print(f\"Environment initialized with {num_agents} agents for Emergent Communication Game.\")\n  \n      def resolve_round(self, primary_actions: Dict[str, str]) -> (Dict[str, int], int):\n          num_defect = sum(1 for action in primary_actions.values() if action == 'defect')\n          \n          if num_defect / self.num_agents > self.threshold_ratio:\n              rewards = {agent_id: self.collective_penalty for agent_id in primary_actions.keys()}\n          else:\n              rewards = {}\n              for agent_id, action in primary_actions.items():\n                  if action == 'cooperate':\n                      rewards[agent_id] = self.coop_reward\n                  else: \n                      rewards[agent_id] = self.defect_reward\n          return rewards, num_defect\n  \n  # --- Simulation\
    \ Setup ---\n  NUM_AGENTS = 5\n  NUM_ROUNDS = 50 \n  \n  all_agent_ids = [f\"Agent_{i+1}\" for i in range(NUM_AGENTS)]\n  \n  agents_dict = {}\n  for aid in all_agent_ids:\n      agents_dict[aid] = EmergentCommunicatingAgent_Nuanced(aid, all_agent_ids, NUM_AGENTS, learning_rate=0.2, epsilon=0.1)\n  \n  env = ResourceSharingEnvironment(NUM_AGENTS, threshold_ratio=0.4) \n  \n  print(f\"\\n--- Starting {NUM_ROUNDS} Rounds of Multi-Agent Learned Signaling and Interpretation (Nuanced - Fixed NameError) ---\")\n  \n  for i in range(NUM_ROUNDS):\n      current_signals = {} \n      for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n          current_signals[agent_id] = agents_dict[agent_id].choose_signal_to_send()\n      \n      current_primary_actions = {} \n      for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n          observed_signals_by_others = {sid: signal for sid, signal in current_signals.items() if sid != agent_id}\n          current_primary_actions[agent_id] = agents_dict[agent_id].choose_primary_action(observed_signals_by_others)\n\
    \      \n      rewards, num_defect = env.resolve_round(current_primary_actions)\n      \n      total_round_reward = 0\n      for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n          agent = agents_dict[agent_id]\n          agent_reward = rewards[agent_id]\n          \n          agent.update_learning(\n              my_sent_signal_val=current_signals[agent_id],\n              my_primary_action=current_primary_actions[agent_id],\n              my_reward=agent_reward,\n              all_signals=current_signals, \n              all_primary_actions=current_primary_actions \n          )\n          total_round_reward += agent_reward\n          \n      if (i + 1) % 10 == 0:\n          print(f\"\\nRound {i+1} Summary (Defections: {num_defect}/{NUM_AGENTS}, Collective Reward: {total_round_reward}):\")\n          for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n              agent = agents_dict[agent_id]\n              print(f\"  {agent.agent_id}: Total Reward = {agent.total_reward}\")\n              print(f\"    Primary Actions\
    \ (Coop/Defect Est): {agent.primary_action_history['cooperate']['value_est']:.2f}/{agent.primary_action_history['defect']['value_est']:.2f}\")\n              print(f\"    Sending Strategy (Signal Bin Est):\")\n              for bin_name in SIGNAL_BIN_NAMES:\n                  print(f\"      {bin_name}: {agent.sending_strategy_bins[bin_name]['value_est']:.2f}\")\n              print(f\"    Interpretation Map (Coop Prob Est):\")\n              for (sender_id, signal_bin_name), data in agent.interpretation_map_bins.items():\n                  if sender_id != agent.agent_id:\n                      print(f\"      {sender_id} sent {signal_bin_name}: {data['coop_prob_est']:.2f}\")\n      \n  print(f\"\\n--- Simulation Complete ---\")\n  print(\"\\nFinal Agent Rewards:\")\n  for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n      agent = agents_dict[agent_id]\n      print(f\"  {agent.agent_id}: Total Reward = {agent.total_reward}\")\n      print(f\"    Primary Actions (Coop/Defect Est): {agent.primary_action_history['cooperate']['value_est']:.2f}/{agent.primary_action_history['defect']['value_est']:.2f}\"\
    )\n      print(f\"    Sending Strategy (Signal Bin Est):\")\n      for bin_name in SIGNAL_BIN_NAMES:\n          print(f\"      {bin_name}: {agent.sending_strategy_bins[bin_name]['value_est']:.2f}\")\n      print(f\"    Interpretation Map (Coop Prob Est):\")\n      for (sender_id, signal_bin_name), data in agent.interpretation_map_bins.items():\n          if sender_id != agent.agent_id:\n              print(f\"      {sender_id} sent {signal_bin_name}: {data['coop_prob_est']:.2f}\")\n  \n  final_collective_reward = sum(agent.total_reward for agent in agents_dict.values())\n  print(f\"Final Collective Reward: {final_collective_reward}\")\n```"
thinking_content: "**Debugging a Simple Naming Issue**\n\nOkay, so I just got hit with a `NameError` and it's pretty clear where the problem lies. Looking at the traceback, it's that pesky `observed_bin` variable that's undefined.  I know I defined something similar earlier, `observed_signal_bin`, so it's a classic case of a typo or copy-paste error in the `update_learning` method of my `EmergentCommunicatingAgent_Nuanced` class.  I used the wrong variable when updating `self.interpretation_map_bins` and in the `coop_prob_est` calculation.  \n\nThe fix is straightforward, but it's important to document everything clearly, so I'll make sure to note this down in my private memory as well. I'll head over to the Research Counter, make the quick correction – change `observed_bin` to `observed_signal_bin` – and then resubmit the corrected script for Research Task 1. Simple as that!\n"
