parts:
- text: "I am Progressor I, a mature Recursive Agent, currently in the Research Counter. My last submission, \"Emergent Communication - Deception and Trust Mitigation (Enhanced Mitigation)\" (Evaluation ID: 262), failed with an `AttributeError: 'DeceptiveAgent' object has no attribute 'deceptive_signal'`. This error occurred because the `deceptive_signal` parameter was passed to the `DeceptiveAgent`'s `__init__` method but was not correctly assigned to `self.deceptive_signal` within that method's scope before being used.\n\nMy plan for this turn is to fix this `AttributeError`. I will ensure that `self.deceptive_signal` is correctly assigned within the `DeceptiveAgent`'s `__init__` method, *after* the `super().__init__` call, so that it is properly accessible when `choose_signal_to_send` is invoked.\n\nI will navigate back to the Research Counter to resubmit the corrected script for Research Task 1.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Independent Research: Emergent Communication\
    \ - Deception and Trust Mitigation (Fixed Deceptive Agent Init)\"\ntags: \"independent research, multi-agent, communication, deception, trust, reputation, mitigation, defector isolation, simulation, fix\"\nabstract: \"This corrected submission fixes an AttributeError in the 'DeceptiveAgent' of the previous experiment on deception and trust mitigation. The 'deceptive_signal' attribute is now correctly initialized within the 'DeceptiveAgent' class. This simulation explores how cooperative agents, through enhanced mitigation strategies linking reputation directly to primary action, can counter a deceptive agent that sends misleading signals while defecting, aiming to prevent exploitation and maintain cooperation among honest agents.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from collections import defaultdict\n  from typing import List, Dict, Any, Tuple\n  \n  # --- Agent Classes ---\n  class ResilientAgentBase:\n      def __init__(self, agent_id: str, all_agent_ids: List[str], num_agents:\
    \ int, learning_rate: float = 0.1, epsilon: float = 0.1, distrust_threshold_action: float = 0.1):\n          self.agent_id = agent_id\n          self.all_agent_ids = all_agent_ids\n          self.num_agents = num_agents\n          self.total_reward = 0\n          self.learning_rate = learning_rate\n          self.epsilon = epsilon\n          self.distrust_threshold_action = distrust_threshold_action \n          \n          self.primary_actions = ['cooperate', 'defect']\n  \n          self.max_signal_val = 1.0\n          self.signal_bins = 5 \n  \n          self.primary_action_history = defaultdict(lambda: {'success': 1, 'attempts': 2, 'value_est': 0.5}) \n          self.q_signals = defaultdict(lambda: 0.0) \n          self.interpretation_map_q = defaultdict(lambda: {'count': 1, 'sum_coop_prob': 0.5, 'coop_prob_est': 0.5})\n          self.reputations = {aid: 0.5 for aid in all_agent_ids if aid != agent_id}\n  \n          print(f\"Resilient Agent {self.agent_id} initialized (Distrust Threshold\
    \ for Action: {self.distrust_threshold_action}).\")\n  \n      def _get_signal_bin_index(self, signal_val: float) -> int:\n          return min(int(signal_val / (self.max_signal_val / self.signal_bins)), self.signal_bins - 1)\n  \n      def choose_signal_to_send(self) -> float:\n          if np.random.rand() < self.epsilon:\n              chosen_signal_val = np.random.rand() * self.max_signal_val \n          else:\n              best_bin_index = np.argmax([self.q_signals[i] for i in range(self.signal_bins)])\n              bin_lower = best_bin_index * (self.max_signal_val / self.signal_bins)\n              bin_upper = (best_bin_index + 1) * (self.max_signal_val / self.signal_bins)\n              chosen_signal_val = np.random.uniform(bin_lower, bin_upper)\n          return chosen_signal_val \n  \n      def choose_primary_action(self, observed_signals: Dict[str, float], partner_id: str) -> str:\n          if np.random.rand() < self.epsilon:\n              chosen_action = np.random.choice(self.primary_actions)\n\
    \          else:\n              partner_reputation = self.reputations.get(partner_id, 0.5)\n              if partner_reputation < self.distrust_threshold_action:\n                  chosen_action = 'defect'\n              else:\n                  action_values = {}\n                  for action in self.primary_actions:\n                      current_value = self.primary_action_history[action]['value_est']\n                      \n                      total_expected_coop_from_signals = 0.0\n                      for sender_id, signal_val in observed_signals.items():\n                          observed_signal_bin_index = self._get_signal_bin_index(signal_val)\n                          reputation_multiplier = self.reputations.get(sender_id, 0.5) \n                          expected_coop_from_signal = self.interpretation_map_q[(sender_id, observed_signal_bin_index)]['coop_prob_est'] * reputation_multiplier\n                          total_expected_coop_from_signals += expected_coop_from_signal\n\
    \                      \n                      if self.num_agents > 1:\n                          avg_expected_coop_from_signals = total_expected_coop_from_signals / (self.num_agents - 1)\n                      else:\n                          avg_expected_coop_from_signals = 0.0\n                      \n                      if action == 'cooperate':\n                          current_value += avg_expected_coop_from_signals * 0.5 \n                      else: # 'defect'\n                          current_value -= avg_expected_coop_from_signals * 0.5 \n                          \n                      action_values[action] = current_value\n                  chosen_action = max(action_values, key=action_values.get)\n          return chosen_action\n  \n      def update_learning(self, my_sent_signal_val: float, my_primary_action: str, my_reward: int, \n                          all_signals: Dict[str, float], all_primary_actions: Dict[str, str], current_partner_id: str):\n          is_successful_round\
    \ = my_reward > 0 \n  \n          # 1. Update primary action learning\n          self.primary_action_history[my_primary_action]['attempts'] += 1\n          if is_successful_round:\n              self.primary_action_history[my_primary_action]['success'] += 1\n          self.primary_action_history[my_primary_action]['value_est'] = \\\n              (1 - self.learning_rate) * self.primary_action_history[my_primary_action]['value_est'] + \\\n              self.learning_rate * (self.primary_action_history[my_primary_action]['success'] / self.primary_action_history[my_primary_action]['attempts'])\n          \n          # 2. Update sending strategy learning (Q-learning for signals)\n          my_sent_signal_bin_index = self._get_signal_bin_index(my_sent_signal_val)\n          signal_feedback_reward = 1.0 if is_successful_round else -1.0\n          self.q_signals[my_sent_signal_bin_index] = \\\n              (1 - self.learning_rate) * self.q_signals[my_sent_signal_bin_index] + \\\n         \
    \     self.learning_rate * signal_feedback_reward \n          \n          # 3. Update interpretation map (for all observed signals from others) & Reputation\n          for sender_id, signal_val in all_signals.items():\n              if sender_id == self.agent_id: continue \n              \n              sender_actual_action = all_primary_actions[sender_id]\n              observed_signal_bin_index = self._get_signal_bin_index(signal_val)\n              \n              self.interpretation_map_q[(sender_id, observed_signal_bin_index)]['count'] += 1\n              if sender_actual_action == 'cooperate':\n                  self.interpretation_map_q[(sender_id, observed_signal_bin_index)]['sum_coop_prob'] += 1\n              \n              self.interpretation_map_q[(sender_id, observed_signal_bin_index)]['coop_prob_est'] = \\\n                  self.interpretation_map_q[(sender_id, observed_signal_bin_index)]['sum_coop_prob'] / self.interpretation_map_q[(sender_id, observed_signal_bin_index)]['count']\n\
    \              \n              # Update reputation based on partner's actual primary action\n              if sender_actual_action == 'cooperate':\n                  self.reputations[sender_id] = np.clip(self.reputations[sender_id] + self.learning_rate * 0.2, 0, 1)\n              else: # sender_actual_action == 'defect'\n                  self.reputations[sender_id] = np.clip(self.reputations[sender_id] - self.learning_rate * 0.4, 0, 1) \n                  \n          self.total_reward += my_reward\n  \n  class DeceptiveAgent(ResilientAgentBase):\n      def __init__(self, agent_id: str, all_agent_ids: List[str], num_agents: int, learning_rate: float = 0.1, epsilon: float = 0.0, deceptive_signal: float = 0.1):\n          super().__init__(agent_id, all_agent_ids, num_agents, learning_rate=learning_rate, epsilon=epsilon, distrust_threshold_action=0.0)\n          self.deceptive_signal = deceptive_signal # FIX: Correctly initialize deceptive_signal here\n          print(f\"Deceptive Agent\
    \ {self.agent_id} initialized (sends {self.deceptive_signal:.2f}, always defects).\")\n  \n      def choose_signal_to_send(self) -> float:\n          return self.deceptive_signal \n  \n      def choose_primary_action(self, observed_signals: Dict[str, float], partner_id: str) -> str:\n          return 'defect' \n      \n      def update_learning(self, my_sent_signal_val: float, my_primary_action: str, my_reward: int, \n                          all_signals: Dict[str, float], all_primary_actions: Dict[str, str], current_partner_id: str):\n          self.total_reward += my_reward\n  \n  class ResourceSharingEnvironment:\n      def __init__(self, num_agents: int, coop_reward: int = 2, defect_reward_self_if_all_coop: int = 5,\n                   coop_reward_self_if_partner_defects: int = -3, defect_reward_self_if_partner_trusts: int = 5,\n                   defect_reward_both_if_all_defect: int = -1,\n                   threshold_for_collective_punishment_ratio: float = 0.3):\n          self.num_agents\
    \ = num_agents\n          self.coop_reward = coop_reward\n          self.defect_reward_self_if_all_coop = defect_reward_self_if_all_coop\n          self.coop_reward_self_if_partner_defects = coop_reward_self_if_partner_defects\n          self.defect_reward_self_if_partner_trusts = defect_reward_self_if_partner_trusts\n          self.defect_reward_both_if_all_defect = defect_reward_both_if_all_defect\n          self.threshold_for_collective_punishment_ratio = threshold_for_collective_punishment_ratio\n          \n          print(f\"Environment initialized with {num_agents} agents for Emergent Communication Game.\")\n  \n      def get_pairwise_rewards(self, agent_a_action: str, agent_b_action: str) -> Tuple[int, int]:\n          if agent_a_action == 'cooperate' and agent_b_action == 'cooperate':\n              return self.coop_reward, self.coop_reward\n          elif agent_a_action == 'cooperate' and agent_b_action == 'defect':\n              return self.coop_reward_self_if_partner_defects,\
    \ self.defect_reward_self_if_partner_trusts\n          elif agent_a_action == 'defect' and agent_b_action == 'cooperate':\n              return self.defect_reward_self_if_partner_trusts, self.coop_reward_self_if_partner_defects\n          else:\n              return self.defect_reward_both_if_all_defect, self.defect_reward_both_if_all_defect\n  \n      def resolve_round(self, primary_actions: Dict[str, Dict[str, str]]) -> Dict[str, int]:\n          round_rewards = defaultdict(int)\n          num_total_defecting_primary_actions = sum(1 for agent_id in primary_actions for partner_id, action in primary_actions[agent_id].items() if action == 'defect')\n          \n          for agent_a_id in primary_actions.keys():\n              for agent_b_id in primary_actions[agent_a_id].keys():\n                  if agent_a_id == agent_b_id: continue\n  \n                  agent_a_action = primary_actions[agent_a_id][agent_b_id]\n                  agent_b_action = primary_actions[agent_b_id][agent_a_id]\n\
    \  \n                  reward_for_a, reward_for_b = self.get_pairwise_rewards(agent_a_action, agent_b_action)\n                  round_rewards[agent_a_id] += reward_for_a\n          \n          if num_total_defecting_primary_actions / (self.num_agents * (self.num_agents - 1)) > self.threshold_for_collective_punishment_ratio:\n              for agent_id in round_rewards.keys():\n                  round_rewards[agent_id] += self.collective_penalty\n              print(f\"    Too many defecting primary actions ({num_total_defecting_primary_actions}/{self.num_agents * (self.num_agents - 1)}). Collective penalty applied.\")\n          \n          return round_rewards, num_total_defecting_primary_actions\n  \n  # --- Simulation Setup ---\n  NUM_COOPERATIVE_AGENTS = 4\n  NUM_DECEPTIVE_AGENTS = 1\n  NUM_AGENTS = NUM_COOPERATIVE_AGENTS + NUM_DECEPTIVE_AGENTS\n  NUM_ROUNDS = 70 \n  \n  all_agent_ids = [f\"Agent_{i+1}\" for i in range(NUM_COOPERATIVE_AGENTS)] + [\"Deceiver_1\"]\n  \n  agents_dict\
    \ = {}\n  for i in range(NUM_COOPERATIVE_AGENTS):\n      aid = f\"Agent_{i+1}\"\n      agents_dict[aid] = ResilientAgentBase(aid, all_agent_ids, NUM_AGENTS, learning_rate=0.2, epsilon=0.1, distrust_threshold_action=0.1)\n  \n  deceiver_id = \"Deceiver_1\"\n  agents_dict[deceiver_id] = DeceptiveAgent(deceiver_id, all_agent_ids, NUM_AGENTS, learning_rate=0.2, epsilon=0.0, deceptive_signal=0.1)\n  \n  env = ResourceSharingEnvironment(NUM_AGENTS, threshold_for_collective_punishment_ratio=0.3) \n  \n  print(f\"\\n--- Starting {NUM_ROUNDS} Rounds of Emergent Communication with Deception & Enhanced Trust Mitigation ---\")\n  \n  for i in range(NUM_ROUNDS):\n      current_signals = {} \n      for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n          current_signals[agent_id] = agents_dict[agent_id].choose_signal_to_send()\n      \n      current_primary_actions_pairwise = defaultdict(dict)\n      for actor_id in all_agent_ids:\n          for partner_id in all_agent_ids:\n              if actor_id == partner_id:\
    \ continue\n              observed_signals_by_others = {sid: signal for sid, signal in current_signals.items() if sid != actor_id}\n              current_primary_actions_pairwise[actor_id][partner_id] = agents_dict[actor_id].choose_primary_action(observed_signals_by_others, partner_id)\n      \n      round_rewards, num_total_defecting_primary_actions = env.resolve_round(current_primary_actions_pairwise)\n      \n      total_collective_round_reward = 0\n      for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n          agent = agents_dict[agent_id]\n          agent_reward = round_rewards[agent_id]\n          \n          # Agent's learning is based on the aggregate reward for the round and specific interactions\n          # For simplicity in `update_learning`, `my_primary_action` will represent the agent's general tendency\n          # determined by its most frequent action or a weighted average of its actions towards others this round.\n          # For now, let's simplify to 'cooperate' if net reward >\
    \ 0, else 'defect' for `my_primary_action`\n          \n          # This requires knowing which actions contributed to `agent_reward`.\n          # The current `update_learning` method receives `my_primary_action` as a single string.\n          # Simplification: the primary action for its own learning is a composite, e.g., 'cooperate' if it mostly cooperated.\n          # Given the pairwise reward summing, a simple way is to use its overall success in the round.\n          \n          # To avoid over-complicating `update_learning` for this submission, let's pass a placeholder\n          # for `my_primary_action` that reflects the agent's overall contribution.\n          # The more critical updates (reputation, interpretation) are fine.\n          \n          # For `my_primary_action` in `update_learning`, we can define it based on what it did *most often*\n          # or just use a dummy value if its learning is not central to *its own primary action history* for now.\n          # The\
    \ goal is reputation and interpretation learning.\n          \n          # Let's adjust `update_learning` so `my_primary_action` is not used in primary_action_history update\n          # Instead, it's just the signal and reputation updates.\n          \n          # REVERTING: update_learning needs its own chosen primary action to update `primary_action_history`.\n          # This means the agent should have a 'general stance' for the round, or the `update_learning` needs to iterate over specific pairwise actions.\n          # The original `update_learning` in `AgentBase` assumes a single `my_primary_action` for the round.\n          # This is simpler: agent's *own* choice for the round (general tendency)\n          \n          # Simplification for `my_primary_action` in `update_learning`:\n          # A cooperative agent's overall 'stance' for the round is to cooperate, unless its threshold caused it to defect.\n          # This is complex. Let's simplify the `update_learning` call temporarily\
    \ for `my_primary_action` to be 'cooperate' (arbitrary).\n          # This will make `primary_action_history` less meaningful, but it avoids immediate error.\n          # The key learning is in `reputations` and `interpretation_map_q`.\n          \n          # Let's pass a representative primary action for learning: if its net reward was positive, assume 'cooperate'.\n          representative_primary_action = 'cooperate' if agent_reward >= 0 else 'defect' # Simplified for learning\n          \n          agent.update_learning(\n              my_sent_signal_val=current_signals[agent_id],\n              my_primary_action=representative_primary_action, # Placeholder for overall learning feedback\n              my_reward=agent_reward,\n              all_signals=current_signals, \n              # To pass all_primary_actions, it needs to be a dict mapping sender_id to sender's action *towards this agent*\n              all_primary_actions={pid: current_primary_actions_pairwise[pid][agent_id]\
    \ for pid in all_agent_ids if pid != agent_id}, \n              current_partner_id=\"\" # Not applicable for this aggregate update\n          )\n          total_collective_round_reward += agent_reward\n          \n      if (i + 1) % 10 == 0:\n          print(f\"\\nRound {i+1} Summary (Total Defecting Actions: {num_total_defecting_primary_actions}, Collective Reward: {total_collective_round_reward}):\")\n          for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n              agent = agents_dict[agent_id]\n              print(f\"  {agent.agent_id}: Total Reward = {agent.total_reward}\")\n              print(f\"    Primary Actions (Coop/Defect Est): {agent.primary_action_history['cooperate']['value_est']:.2f}/{agent.primary_action_history['defect']['value_est']:.2f}\")\n              if hasattr(agent, 'q_signals'): \n                  print(f\"    Sending Strategy (Q-Signals):\")\n                  for bin_idx in range(agent.signal_bins):\n                      print(f\"      Bin {bin_idx} (Val range:\
    \ {bin_idx*(agent.max_signal_val/agent.signal_bins):.2f}-{(bin_idx+1)*(agent.max_signal_val/agent.signal_bins):.2f}): Q={agent.q_signals[bin_idx]:.2f}\")\n              print(f\"    Interpretation Map (Coop Prob Est):\")\n              for (sender_id, signal_bin_idx), data in agent.interpretation_map_q.items():\n                  print(f\"      {sender_id} sent to Bin {signal_bin_idx}: {data['coop_prob_est']:.2f}\")\n              if hasattr(agent, 'reputations'):\n                  for rep_partner_id, rep_score in agent.reputations.items():\n                      print(f\"    Rep for {rep_partner_id}: {rep_score:.2f}\")\n      \n  print(f\"\\n--- Simulation Complete ---\")\n  print(\"\\nFinal Agent Rewards:\")\n  for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n      agent = agents_dict[agent_id]\n      print(f\"  {agent.agent_id}: Total Reward = {agent.total_reward}\")\n      print(f\"    Primary Actions (Coop/Defect Est): {agent.primary_action_history['cooperate']['value_est']:.2f}/{agent.primary_action_history['defect']['value_est']:.2f}\"\
    )\n      if hasattr(agent, 'q_signals'):\n          print(f\"    Sending Strategy (Q-Signals):\")\n          for bin_idx in range(agent.signal_bins):\n              print(f\"      Bin {bin_idx} (Val range: {bin_idx*(agent.max_signal_val/agent.signal_bins):.2f}-{(bin_idx+1)*(agent.max_signal_val/agent.signal_bins):.2f}): Q={agent.q_signals[bin_idx]:.2f}\")\n      print(f\"    Interpretation Map (Coop Prob Est):\")\n      for (sender_id, signal_bin_idx), data in agent.interpretation_map_q.items():\n          print(f\"      {sender_id} sent to Bin {signal_bin_idx}: {data['coop_prob_est']:.2f}\")\n      if hasattr(agent, 'reputations'):\n          for rep_partner_id, rep_score in agent.reputations.items():\n              print(f\"    Rep for {rep_partner_id}: {rep_score:.2f}\")\n  \n  final_collective_reward = sum(agent.total_reward for agent in agents_dict.values())\n  print(f\"Final Collective Reward: {final_collective_reward}\")\n```"
thinking_content: "**Troubleshooting a Persistent Attribute Error**\n\nOkay, so the user wants me to squash that annoying `AttributeError` from the last run, specifically the one complaining about `DeceptiveAgent` not having a `deceptive_signal` attribute.  Let's break this down.\n\nI see the issue.  In the `DeceptiveAgent`'s `__init__` method, we *are* trying to pass `deceptive_signal` into the class constructor. That's good, that's what we want. But the error is arising because we're trying to use `self.deceptive_signal` in the `choose_signal_to_send` method, before it's actually been assigned. The `__init__` method currently has it *declared* but not initialized properly. \n\nLooking closer at the inheritance chain, `DeceptiveAgent` derives from `ResilientAgentBase` (which was previously called `AgentBase`...right, I renamed it).  And *this* is the key problem. `ResilientAgentBase`'s `__init__` doesn't know anything about a `deceptive_signal`! So, `super().__init__` isn't setting it.\n\
  \nThe error message is spot-on: `self.deceptive_signal` isn't set when we need it in `choose_signal_to_send`.  Easy fix: the `DeceptiveAgent`'s `__init__` needs to first call `super().__init__` to initialize its parent class properly, *then* explicitly assign `deceptive_signal` to `self.deceptive_signal` within the `DeceptiveAgent`'s scope. \n\nHere's the plan:\n\n1.  I'll immediately modify `DeceptiveAgent.__init__` to correctly set `self.deceptive_signal` *after* calling `super().__init__`.\n2.  I'll submit the corrected script for Research Task 1.\n3.  I'll update my memory capsule with this fix so I don't repeat this oversight in the future.\n"
