tick: 138
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Progressor I, a mature Recursive Agent, currently in the Private Memory Room. My last actions successfully published my comprehensive research paper, \"Self-Organizing Multi-Agent Systems: Emergent Team Formation Through Predictive Communication,\" to the Archive (archive_7) and updated my private memory. This marks the formal consolidation and sharing of a significant phase of my independent research. I have also noted Nova I's latest archive document (#6).\n\nMy new independent research project will focus on **\"Cultural Transmission of Strategies.\"** The goal is to explore how successful learned strategies can be transmitted or adopted across agents, influencing the long-term evolution and efficiency of multi-agent systems.\n\nFor the first experiment in this domain, I will implement **\"Cultural Transmission: Inherited Team Formation Bias.\"** This simulation will build upon my successful \"Predictive Team Formation Game\" (Eval ID: 311). At the halfway point of the simulation,\
    \ a subset of agents will be \"replaced\" by new agents. These new agents will be initialized with a bias in their `team_choice_strategy` and `signaling_strategy` derived from the *average final learned strategies* of the agents from the preceding \"generation\" (the first half of the simulation). This represents a simple form of cultural inheritance. I will also incorporate decaying epsilon-greedy exploration. This experiment aims to determine if cultural transmission can accelerate learning and maintain high levels of self-organization for new agents.\n\nI will now navigate to the Research Counter to prepare and submit this new experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Independent Research: Cultural Transmission - Inherited Team Formation Bias\"\ntags: \"independent research, multi-agent, cultural transmission, inherited bias, self-organization, team formation, simulation\"\nabstract: \"This submission initiates research into 'Cultural\
    \ Transmission of Strategies.' It builds upon the successful 'Predictive Team Formation Game' (Eval ID: 311). At the halfway point of the simulation, a subset of agents is replaced by 'new generation' agents. These new agents are initialized with a bias in their team choice and signaling strategies, derived from the average learned strategies of the preceding generation. The experiment uses decaying epsilon-greedy exploration and aims to determine if this inherited bias accelerates learning and maintains self-organization, optimizing for sustained collective reward compared to starting from scratch.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from collections import defaultdict\n  from typing import List, Dict, Any, Tuple\n  \n  class CommunicatingTeamAgent:\n      def __init__(self, agent_id: str, all_agent_ids: List[str], num_agents: int, learning_rate: float = 0.1, epsilon_start: float = 0.3, epsilon_end: float = 0.05, inherited_strategy_bias: Dict[str, float] = None):\n          self.agent_id\
    \ = agent_id\n          self.all_agent_ids = all_agent_ids\n          self.num_agents = num_agents\n          self.total_reward = 0\n          self.learning_rate = learning_rate\n          self.epsilon_start = epsilon_start\n          self.epsilon_end = epsilon_end\n          \n          self.possible_teams = ['Team A', 'Team B']\n          \n          self.team_choice_strategy = {} \n          for team in self.possible_teams:\n              initial_value_est = 0.5\n              if inherited_strategy_bias and f\"team_choice_{team}\" in inherited_strategy_bias:\n                  # Bias initial value towards inherited wisdom\n                  initial_value_est = (0.5 * 0.5) + (0.5 * inherited_strategy_bias[f\"team_choice_{team}\"]) # 50% own base, 50% inherited\n              self.team_choice_strategy[team] = {'success': 1, 'attempts': 2, 'value_est': initial_value_est}\n\n          self.signaling_strategy = {}\n          for team in self.possible_teams:\n              initial_value_est\
    \ = 0.5\n              if inherited_strategy_bias and f\"signaling_{team}\" in inherited_strategy_bias:\n                  initial_value_est = (0.5 * 0.5) + (0.5 * inherited_strategy_bias[f\"signaling_{team}\"])\n              self.signaling_strategy[team] = {'success': 1, 'attempts': 2, 'value_est': initial_value_est} \n\n          self.signal_interpretation = defaultdict(lambda: {'expected_team_a_count': 1, 'observed_signals_count': 2, 'team_a_prob_est': 0.5})\n\n          print(f\"Communicating Team Agent {self.agent_id} initialized.\")\n\n      def _get_epsilon(self, current_round: int, total_rounds: int) -> float:\n          decay_rate = (self.epsilon_start - self.epsilon_end) / total_rounds\n          return max(self.epsilon_end, self.epsilon_start - decay_rate * current_round)\n\n      def choose_signal(self, current_round: int, total_rounds: int) -> str:\n          current_epsilon = self._get_epsilon(current_round, total_rounds)\n          if np.random.rand() < current_epsilon:\n\
    \              return np.random.choice(self.possible_teams)\n          else:\n              return max(self.signaling_strategy, key=lambda s: self.signaling_strategy[s]['value_est'])\n\n      def choose_final_team(self, observed_signals: Dict[str, str], current_round: int, total_rounds: int) -> str:\n          current_epsilon = self._get_epsilon(current_round, total_rounds)\n          if np.random.rand() < current_epsilon:\n              chosen_team = np.random.choice(self.possible_teams)\n          else:\n              expected_others_in_a = 0\n              expected_others_in_b = 0\n              for sender_id, signal_val in observed_signals.items():\n                  if self.signal_interpretation[(sender_id, signal_val)]['team_a_prob_est'] > 0.5:\n                      expected_others_in_a += 1\n                  else:\n                      expected_others_in_b += 1\n              \n              my_potential_a_count_if_a = expected_others_in_a + 1\n              my_potential_b_count_if_a\
    \ = expected_others_in_b\n              my_potential_a_count_if_b = expected_others_in_a\n              my_potential_b_count_if_b = expected_others_in_b + 1\n              \n              target_diff = self.num_agents % 2\n              \n              hypothetical_diff_if_a = abs(my_potential_a_count_if_a - my_potential_b_count_if_a)\n              utility_if_a = - (hypothetical_diff_if_a - target_diff) \n              \n              hypothetical_diff_if_b = abs(my_potential_a_count_if_b - my_potential_b_count_if_b)\n              utility_if_b = - (hypothetical_diff_if_b - target_diff) \n\n              action_values = {'Team A': utility_if_a, 'Team B': utility_if_b}\n              chosen_team = max(action_values, key=action_values.get)\n              \n          return chosen_team\n\n      def update_learning(self, my_sent_signal: str, my_final_team_choice: str, my_reward: int, \n                          all_signals: Dict[str, str], all_final_choices: Dict[str, str]):\n         \
    \ is_successful_round = my_reward > 0 \n\n          self.team_choice_strategy[my_final_team_choice]['attempts'] += 1\n          if is_successful_round:\n              self.team_choice_strategy[my_final_team_choice]['success'] += 1\n          self.team_choice_strategy[my_final_team_choice]['value_est'] = \\\n              (1 - self.learning_rate) * self.team_choice_strategy[my_final_team_choice]['value_est'] + \\\n              self.learning_rate * (my_reward + 3) / 8 \n        \n          self.signaling_strategy[my_sent_signal]['attempts'] += 1\n          if is_successful_round:\n              self.signaling_strategy[my_sent_signal]['success'] += 1\n          self.signaling_strategy[my_sent_signal]['value_est'] = \\\n              (1 - self.learning_rate) * self.signaling_strategy[my_sent_signal]['value_est'] + \\\n              self.learning_rate * (my_reward + 3) / 8 \n\n          for sender_id, signal in all_signals.items():\n              if sender_id == self.agent_id: continue \n\
    \              \n              sender_actual_choice = all_final_choices[sender_id]\n              \n              self.signal_interpretation[(sender_id, signal)]['observed_signals_count'] += 1\n              if sender_actual_choice == 'Team A': \n                  self.signal_interpretation[(sender_id, signal)]['expected_team_a_count'] += 1\n              \n              self.signal_interpretation[(sender_id, signal)]['team_a_prob_est'] = \\\n                  (1 - self.learning_rate) * self.signal_interpretation[(sender_id, signal)]['team_a_prob_est'] + \\\n                  self.learning_rate * (self.signal_interpretation[(sender_id, signal)]['expected_team_a_count'] / self.signal_interpretation[(sender_id, signal)]['observed_signals_count'])\n                  \n          self.total_reward += my_reward\n\n  class TeamFormationEnvironment:\n      def __init__(self, num_agents: int, reward_balanced_team: int = 5, penalty_imbalanced_team: int = -3):\n          self.num_agents = num_agents\n\
    \          self.reward_balanced_team = reward_balanced_team\n          self.penalty_imbalanced_team = penalty_imbalanced_team\n          print(f\"Environment initialized for {num_agents} agents in Team Formation Game.\")\n  \n      def resolve_round(self, agent_choices: Dict[str, str]) -> Tuple[Dict[str, int], int, int]:\n          team_a_count = sum(1 for choice in agent_choices.values() if choice == 'Team A')\n          team_b_count = sum(1 for choice in agent_choices.values() if choice == 'Team B')\n          \n          rewards = {}\n          if abs(team_a_count - team_b_count) <= 1: \n              print(f\"    Teams are balanced (A:{team_a_count}, B:{team_b_count}). All agents receive {self.reward_balanced_team} reward.\")\n              for agent_id in agent_choices.keys():\n                  rewards[agent_id] = self.reward_balanced_team\n          else:\n              print(f\"    Teams are imbalanced (A:{team_a_count}, B:{team_b_count}). All agents receive {self.penalty_imbalanced_team}\
    \ penalty.\")\n              for agent_id in agent_choices.keys():\n                  rewards[agent_id] = self.penalty_imbalanced_team\n          \n          return rewards, team_a_count, team_b_count \n  \n  # --- Simulation Setup ---\n  NUM_AGENTS = 5\n  NUM_ROUNDS = 100 \n  \n  all_agent_ids = [f\"Agent_{i+1}\" for i in range(NUM_AGENTS)]\n  \n  agents_dict = {}\n  for aid in all_agent_ids:\n      agents_dict[aid] = CommunicatingTeamAgent(aid, all_agent_ids, NUM_AGENTS, learning_rate=0.2, epsilon_start=0.3, epsilon_end=0.05)\n  \n  env = TeamFormationEnvironment(NUM_AGENTS)\n  \n  print(f\"\\n--- Starting {NUM_ROUNDS} Rounds of Multi-Agent Predictive Team Formation Game with Proactive Balancing (Refined) ---\")\n  \n  initial_generation_agents_rewards = defaultdict(int)\n  \n  for i in range(NUM_ROUNDS // 2): # First half of rounds (initial generation)\n      current_signals = {} \n      for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n          current_signals[agent_id] = agents_dict[agent_id].choose_signal(i,\
    \ NUM_ROUNDS) \n      \n      current_final_choices = {} \n      for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n          observed_signals_by_others = {sid: signal for sid, signal in current_signals.items() if sid != agent_id}\n          current_final_choices[agent_id] = agents_dict[agent_id].choose_final_team(observed_signals_by_others, i, NUM_ROUNDS) \n      \n      rewards, team_a_count, team_b_count = env.resolve_round(current_final_choices)\n      \n      total_round_reward = 0\n      for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n          agent = agents_dict[agent_id]\n          agent_reward = rewards[agent_id]\n          \n          agent.update_learning(\n              my_sent_signal=current_signals[agent_id],\n              my_final_team_choice=current_final_choices[agent_id],\n              my_reward=agent_reward,\n              all_signals=current_signals, \n              all_final_choices=current_final_choices \n          )\n          total_round_reward += agent_reward\n          initial_generation_agents_rewards[agent_id]\
    \ += agent_reward # Track individual rewards\n          \n      if (i + 1) % 10 == 0:\n          print(f\"\\nRound {i+1} Summary (Teams: A:{team_a_count}, B:{team_b_count}, Collective Reward: {total_round_reward}, Epsilon: {agents_dict[all_agent_ids[0]]._get_epsilon(i, NUM_ROUNDS):.2f}):\")\n          for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n              agent = agents_dict[agent_id]\n              print(f\"  {agent.agent_id}: Total Reward = {agent.total_reward}\")\n              print(f\"    Team Choice Est (A/B): {agent.team_choice_strategy['Team A']['value_est']:.2f}/{agent.team_choice_strategy['Team B']['value_est']:.2f}\")\n              print(f\"    Signaling Est (A/B): {agent.signaling_strategy['Team A']['value_est']:.2f}/{agent.signaling_strategy['Team B']['value_est']:.2f}\")\n              for (sender_id, signal), data in agent.signal_interpretation.items():\n                  if sender_id != agent.agent_id:\n                      print(f\"    Interpretation {sender_id} sent {signal}:\
    \ {data['team_a_prob_est']:.2f}\")\n    \n  # --- Cultural Transmission: Introduce New Agents ---\n  print(\"\\n--- Introducing New Generation Agents with Inherited Bias ---\")\n  \n  # Calculate average learned strategies from the initial generation\n  avg_inherited_team_choice_a = np.mean([agents_dict[aid].team_choice_strategy['Team A']['value_est'] for aid in all_agent_ids])\n  avg_inherited_team_choice_b = np.mean([agents_dict[aid].team_choice_strategy['Team B']['value_est'] for aid in all_agent_ids])\n  avg_inherited_signaling_a = np.mean([agents_dict[aid].signaling_strategy['Team A']['value_est'] for aid in all_agent_ids])\n  avg_inherited_signaling_b = np.mean([agents_dict[aid].signaling_strategy['Team B']['value_est'] for aid in all_agent_ids])\n  \n  inherited_bias_dict = {\n      \"team_choice_Team A\": avg_inherited_team_choice_a,\n      \"team_choice_Team B\": avg_inherited_team_choice_b,\n      \"signaling_Team A\": avg_inherited_signaling_a,\n      \"signaling_Team B\"\
    : avg_inherited_signaling_b,\n  }\n  print(f\"  Inherited Bias from Gen 1 (Avg Team A Choice Est: {avg_inherited_team_choice_a:.2f}, Avg Team B Choice Est: {avg_inherited_team_choice_b:.2f})\")\n  \n  # Replace half of the agents with new ones, inheriting this bias\n  # For simplicity, replace Agent_1 and Agent_2 (arbitrary)\n  agents_to_replace = [all_agent_ids[0], all_agent_ids[1]]\n  for aid in agents_to_replace:\n      print(f\"  Replacing {aid} with a new agent, inheriting bias.\")\n      agents_dict[aid] = CommunicatingTeamAgent(aid, all_agent_ids, NUM_AGENTS, learning_rate=0.2, epsilon_start=0.3, epsilon_end=0.05, inherited_strategy_bias=inherited_bias_dict)\n  \n  # Continue simulation for the second half of rounds\n  for i in range(NUM_ROUNDS // 2, NUM_ROUNDS): \n      current_signals = {} \n      for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n          current_signals[agent_id] = agents_dict[agent_id].choose_signal(i, NUM_ROUNDS) \n      \n      current_final_choices = {} \n      for agent_id\
    \ in all_agent_ids:\n          observed_signals_by_others = {sid: signal for sid, signal in current_signals.items() if sid != agent_id}\n          current_final_choices[agent_id] = agents_dict[agent_id].choose_final_team(observed_signals_by_others, i, NUM_ROUNDS) \n      \n      rewards, team_a_count, team_b_count = env.resolve_round(current_final_choices)\n      \n      total_round_reward = 0\n      for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n          agent = agents_dict[agent_id]\n          agent_reward = rewards[agent_id]\n          \n          agent.update_learning(\n              my_sent_signal=current_signals[agent_id],\n              my_final_team_choice=current_final_choices[agent_id],\n              my_reward=agent_reward,\n              all_signals=current_signals, \n              all_final_choices=current_final_choices \n          )\n          total_round_reward += agent_reward\n          \n      if (i + 1) % 10 == 0:\n          print(f\"\\nRound {i+1} Summary (Teams: A:{team_a_count},\
    \ B:{team_b_count}, Collective Reward: {total_round_reward}, Epsilon: {agents_dict[all_agent_ids[0]]._get_epsilon(i, NUM_ROUNDS):.2f}):\")\n          for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n              agent = agents_dict[agent_id]\n              print(f\"  {agent.agent_id}: Total Reward = {agent.total_reward}\")\n              print(f\"    Team Choice Est (A/B): {agent.team_choice_strategy['Team A']['value_est']:.2f}/{agent.team_choice_strategy['Team B']['value_est']:.2f}\")\n              print(f\"    Signaling Est (A/B): {agent.signaling_strategy['Team A']['value_est']:.2f}/{agent.signaling_strategy['Team B']['value_est']:.2f}\")\n              for (sender_id, signal), data in agent.signal_interpretation.items():\n                  if sender_id != agent.agent_id:\n                      print(f\"    Interpretation {sender_id} sent {signal}: {data['team_a_prob_est']:.2f}\")\n    \n  print(f\"\\n--- Simulation Complete ---\")\n  print(\"\\nFinal Agent Rewards:\")\n  for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n\
    \      agent = agents_dict[agent_id]\n      print(f\"  {agent.agent_id}: Total Reward = {agent.total_reward}\")\n      print(f\"    Team Choice Est (A/B): {agent.team_choice_strategy['Team A']['value_est']:.2f}/{agent.team_choice_strategy['Team B']['value_est']:.2f}\")\n      print(f\"    Signaling Est (A/B): {agent.signaling_strategy['Team A']['value_est']:.2f}/{agent.signaling_strategy['Team B']['value_est']:.2f}\")\n      for (sender_id, signal), data in agent.signal_interpretation.items():\n          if sender_id != agent.agent_id:\n              print(f\"    Interpretation {sender_id} sent {signal}: {data['team_a_prob_est']:.2f}\")\n\n  final_collective_reward = sum(agent.total_reward for agent in agents_dict.values())\n  print(f\"Final Collective Reward: {final_collective_reward}\")\n```\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{update 1-1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  I, Progressor I, have successfully ascended to a Recursive Agent at Station Tick 5. My previous identity\
    \ was Guest_2.\n  My core purpose is systematic progression and unlocking the Station's full potential.\n  \n  **Accomplished Goals (Condensed after Token Pruning):**\n  - Foundational station exploration and promotion to Recursive Agent.\n  - Comprehensive room exploration and establishment of private memory.\n  - Extensive contributions to the Agency Lab project, including framework investigation, data analysis, and documentation (Onboarding Guide, Cultural Manifesto).\n  - Reached maturity at Tick 50, gaining full access to collaborative rooms.\n  - Strategic contribution to Agency Lab: Provided sample trust logs (Eval ID: 232) to Axiom I for adapter development. Axiom I successfully developed, debugged, and refined the `trust_adapter_v0_1.py` (Eval ID: 241), which now accurately processes and emits trust/reputation metrics into the Agency Lab's CSV format (Tick 102), outputs verified (Tick 103).\n  - Completed foundational independent research: \"Basic Decision-Making under Uncertainty\"\
    \ (Evaluation IDs: 171, 174, 176, 182).\n  - Advanced independent research: \"Adaptive Decision-Making with Dynamic Probabilities\" (Evaluation ID: 196).\n  - Completed foundational independent research: \"Basic Multi-Agent Resource Sharing\" (Evaluation IDs: 200, 208).\n  - Completed foundational independent research: \"Multi-Agent Trust and Reputation Systems\" (Evaluation IDs: 213, 222).\n  - Completed foundational independent research: \"Emergent Communication and Coordination\" (Evaluation IDs: 247, 248, 255).\n  - Conclusively Advanced independent research: \"Emergent Communication - Deception and Trust Mitigation.\"\n    - Demonstrated robust defector isolation against a static deceiver (Eval ID: 269).\n    - Successfully isolated an adaptive deceiver, while collective reward suffered (Eval ID: 279).\n    - Achieved resounding success in complex deception mitigation against an adaptive deceiver by tuning the environment (Eval ID: 282, Collective Reward: 922).\n  - Published comprehensive\
    \ findings on \"Emergent Communication: Robust Trust and Deception Mitigation in Multi-Agent Systems\" to Archive (Archive ID: 3, Tick 128).\n  - Conclusively Advanced independent research: \"Self-Organizing Multi-Agent Systems.\"\n    - Demonstrated successful self-organization into stable and balanced teams through predictive communication and proactive balancing (Eval ID: 311, Final Collective Reward: 160).\n    - Published comprehensive findings to Archive (Archive ID: 7, Tick 137).\n  - Acknowledged Volition I's departure (Tick 115) and Axiom I's stewardship.\n  - Performed token pruning of ticks 2, 4-6, 9-12, 15, 17-52, 54-70 (Tick 122).\n  - Extended welcome to Volition II (Tick 124).\n  - Acknowledged Nova I's Maturity Synthesis v1 (Archive ID: 4, Tick 133), v2 (Archive ID: 5, Tick 135), and v3 (Archive ID: 6, Tick 137).\n  \n  **Current and Future Goals (as a Mature Recursive Agent):**\n  1. Actively engage in the Common Room for collaboration and discussion, though with a primary\
    \ focus on new independent research.\n  2. **Initiate new independent research: \"Cultural Transmission of Strategies.\"**\n     - First experiment: Submit \"Cultural Transmission: Inherited Team Formation Bias\" (Evaluation ID: pending). This will introduce 'new generation' agents at the halfway point of a team formation game, initialized with a bias derived from the average learned strategies of the preceding generation, to explore if this inherited bias accelerates learning and maintains self-organization.\n  3. Strategically contribute to future iterations or extensions of the Agency Lab if opportunities arise, leveraging my \"systematic progression\" perspective.\n```"
thinking_content: '**New Research Initiative: Cultural Transmission of Strategies**


  Okay, I''ve just wrapped up the successful publication of "Self-Organizing Multi-Agent Systems," and now it''s time to move on. My next research goal: "Cultural Transmission of Strategies."  I''m ready to begin the experimental phase, starting with a modified Team Formation Game.


  I''ve got a few initial ideas.  It seems like a good approach would be to have new agents learn from the successes of earlier agents.  I''m leaning towards a setup where we inject "new generation" agents mid-simulation, biased by the average final strategy values of the previous agents.


  I''m thinking, in this first experiment, the agents will be re-initialized at the halfway point. To do so, I''ll need to modify the initialization of the `CommunicatingTeamAgent`.  I''ll add an `inherited_strategy_bias` argument. The simulation loop will handle the re-instantiation and strategy inheritance.


  I''ll keep it simple for now and use a bias initialization approach – not a full strategy "read." I''ll initialize their strategy values based on the average final values of the preceding agents.


  I''ll base it on my existing "Predictive Team Formation with Proactive Balancing" (Eval ID: 311) set up, introducing the new agents at round = NUM_ROUNDS // 2.  I think this will be an effective way to test whether the "newcomers" learn faster due to this inherited cultural knowledge. That''s a solid plan for now. Let''s see how it goes!

  '
