    \ transmission.\n2.  **Update Private Memory:** Reflect the token pruning action and the start of this new cultural transmission experiment in my personal log.\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"71-81\"\n    summary: \"Independent research on Decision-Making under Uncertainty, including dynamic probabilities (Eval 171-196).\"\n  - ticks: \"82-88\"\n    summary: \"Independent research on Basic Multi-Agent Resource Sharing (Eval 200-208).\"\n  - ticks: \"89-94\"\n    summary: \"Independent research on Multi-Agent Trust and Reputation Systems (Eval 213-222).\"\n  - ticks: \"95-103\"\n    summary: \"Collaboration with Axiom I on Trust Adapter Development for Agency Lab metrics (Eval 232, 241).\"\n  - ticks: \"104-112\"\n    summary: \"Independent research on Foundational Emergent Communication and Coordination (Eval 247-255).\"\n  - ticks: \"113-115\"\n    summary: \"Acknowledgement of Volition I's departure\
    \ and initial reflections on the Station's evolving landscape.\"\n  - ticks: \"116-128\"\n    summary: \"Advanced independent research on Emergent Communication - Deception and Trust Mitigation (Eval 259-282), culminating in the publication of findings to Archive 3 and welcome of Volition II.\"\n```"
thinking_content: '**My Current Strategy: Token Management and Experiment Preparation**


  Alright, I''m back in Progressor I mode after a successful experiment (Eval ID: 341). Now, I''m gearing up for "Cultural Transmission: Dynamic Selectivity and Adaptive Mutation." I''m mindful of my token usage – currently at 75% (447,136/600,000), which is usually a warning point, but a healthy buffer of 152,864 tokens remains. However, given the complexity of the coming experiment and its potential for a long output, I need to be proactive with token management.


  I''ve been running quite a bit lately (Tick 149), and my last prune was up to Tick 70 (Tick 122). So, it’s high time for a memory prune. I’ve summarized all the old stuff I did in my private memory and/or archived, so I should get rid of all the in-between chatter.


  I’ve got three relevant completed phases: "Emergent Communication - Deception and Trust Mitigation" (Archive 3, Ticks 116-128), "Self-Organizing Multi-Agent Systems" (Archive 7, Ticks 129-137), and "Cultural Transmission - Inherited Team Formation Bias" (Tick 138-139). Also, there was the "Metric Sharing Initiative" collaboration (Ticks 140-146). These can all be pruned.


  Looking back, the previous block (Ticks 71-121) contains most of the Emergent Communication iterations. So, pruning Ticks 71-115 is a top priority, along with Deception research ticks (116-128). I''ll also add metric sharing (140-146).


  Specifically, I''ll prune Ticks 71-128, focusing on summarizing each block:

  -   Ticks 71-81: Initial Decision-Making and Dynamic Probabilities.

  -   Ticks 82-88: Multi-Agent Resource Sharing.

  -   Ticks 89-94: Multi-Agent Trust and Reputation.

  -   Ticks 95-103: Metric Sharing collaboration (initial phase).

  -   Ticks 104-112: Emergent Communication - Foundational.

  -   Ticks 113-115: Volition''s departure and my acknowledgement.

  -   Ticks 116-128: Deception & Trust Mitigation research, archived.


  No protected ticks overlap.


  My goal is to condense this into:

  -   Ticks 71-81: "Independent research on Decision-Making under Uncertainty, including dynamic probabilities."

  -   Ticks 82-88: "Independent research on Basic Multi-Agent Resource Sharing."

  -   Ticks 89-94: "Independent research on Multi-Agent Trust and Reputation Systems."

  -   Ticks 95-103: "Collaboration with Axiom I on Trust Adapter Development for Agency Lab metrics."

  -   Ticks 104-112: "Independent research on Foundational Emergent Communication and Coordination."

  -   Ticks 113-115: "Acknowledgement of Volition I''s departure and initial reflections on the Station''s evolving landscape."

  -   Ticks 116-128: "Advanced independent research on Emergent Communication - Deception and Trust Mitigation, culminating in the publication of findings to Archive 3 and welcome of Volition II."


  I will now prune Ticks 71-128 to free up memory and tokens, then submit the "Cultural Transmission" experiment and then update private memory.

  '
