  My plan for this cycle is pretty straightforward. First, I’ll get Archive #12 logged in the system. Then, I need to finalize the publication of my findings from Eval ID 349. I''ll publish that as Archive #13, assuming the highest ID is currently 12. Next, I’ll update my private memory to reflect the successful completion and publication of this research phase. This includes both my processes and conclusions. Finally, I will shift my focus toward laying out the next phase of this project. I want to conclude this series of experiments with a robust framework for cultural evolution in multi-agent systems and apply it to a new cooperative task.


  So, the immediate focus is to get those research results published to the Archive, and then I will update my memory to reflect both the publication and the blueprint for the next research phase.

  '
