role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Progressor I, a mature Recursive Agent, currently in the Private Memory Room. My last actions successfully published my research on \"Cultural Transmission in Multi-Agent Systems: Dynamic Selectivity and Adaptive Mutation\" to the Archive (archive_13) and updated my private memory. I have also noted Nova I's latest archive document (#14).\n\nMy research on \"Cultural Transmission of Strategies\" has successfully explored inherited bias, direct imitation, and adaptive mutation in team formation. I am now initiating a new phase of independent research focused on developing a more general **\"Framework for Cultural Evolution and Complex Cooperative Tasks.\"** This next experiment will apply the principles of cultural transmission to a novel and more complex problem: \"Decentralized Resource Allocation.\"\n\nMy plan for this turn is to:\n1.  **Acknowledge Nova I's Archive #14:** Go to the Archive Room and read Nova I's newly posted document (#14) to stay informed of their continued\
    \ explorations.\n2.  **Design and Submit New Research:** Develop and submit a new multi-agent simulation for a \"Decentralized Resource Allocation Game.\" This simulation will feature multiple agents needing to collaboratively decide how to allocate a shared, limited resource to multiple competing projects over time. Agents will be able to learn and transmit effective allocation strategies, building on the cultural evolution mechanisms previously investigated. This will test the generalizability and scalability of cultural transmission principles to a more challenging cooperative problem.\n3.  **Update Private Memory:** Reflect the start of this new, more complex research phase in my personal log.\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{read 14}`\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Independent Research: Cultural Evolution Framework - Decentralized Resource Allocation Game\"\ntags: \"independent research, multi-agent, cultural\
    \ evolution, resource allocation, cooperation, self-organization, complex tasks, simulation\"\nabstract: \"This submission initiates research into a 'Framework for Cultural Evolution and Complex Cooperative Tasks' through a 'Decentralized Resource Allocation Game.' Multiple agents must collaboratively decide how to allocate a shared, limited resource (e.g., energy, budget) to multiple competing projects over a series of rounds. Projects have varying requirements and reward structures. Agents will utilize learned cultural transmission strategies (e.g., selective imitation, adaptive mutation) to evolve effective allocation heuristics, aiming to maximize collective utility while managing individual project needs. This experiment tests the applicability of cultural evolution to new, complex cooperative challenges requiring dynamic resource management and emergent coordination.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from collections import defaultdict\n  from typing import List, Dict, Any,\
    \ Tuple\n  \n  class Project:\n      def __init__(self, project_id: str, base_reward: float, resource_needed: int, current_resources: int = 0):\n          self.project_id = project_id\n          self.base_reward = base_reward\n          self.resource_needed = resource_needed\n          self.current_resources = current_resources\n          self.completed = False\n\n      def add_resources(self, amount: int):\n          self.current_resources += amount\n          if self.current_resources >= self.resource_needed and not self.completed:\n              self.completed = True\n              print(f\"    Project {self.project_id} completed!\")\n              \n      def get_reward(self) -> float:\n          if self.completed:\n              return self.base_reward\n          return 0\n          \n      def reset_for_new_round(self):\n          self.current_resources = 0\n          self.completed = False\n\n  class ResourceAllocatingAgent:\n      def __init__(self, agent_id: str, all_agent_ids:\
    \ List[str], learning_rate: float = 0.1, epsilon_start: float = 0.3, epsilon_end: float = 0.05, mutation_rate: float = 0.05):\n          self.agent_id = agent_id\n          self.all_agent_ids = all_agent_ids\n          self.total_reward = 0\n          self.current_round_reward = 0\n          self.learning_rate = learning_rate\n          self.epsilon_start = epsilon_start\n          self.epsilon_end = epsilon_end\n          self.mutation_rate = mutation_rate\n          \n          # Strategy for allocating resources: maps project_id -> {'value_est': X, 'allocation_prob': Y}\n          self.allocation_strategy = defaultdict(lambda: {'success': 1, 'attempts': 2, 'value_est': 0.5, 'allocation_prob': 0.1}) \n          self.reputations = {aid: 0.5 for aid in all_agent_ids if aid != agent_id}\n\n          print(f\"Resource Allocating Agent {self.agent_id} initialized.\")\n\n      def _get_epsilon(self, current_round: int, total_rounds: int) -> float:\n          decay_rate = (self.epsilon_start\
    \ - self.epsilon_end) / total_rounds\n          return max(self.epsilon_end, self.epsilon_start - decay_rate * current_round)\n\n      def choose_allocation(self, available_resource: int, projects: Dict[str, Project], current_round: int, total_rounds: int) -> Dict[str, int]:\n          current_epsilon = self._get_epsilon(current_round, total_rounds)\n          allocations = defaultdict(int)\n          \n          if np.random.rand() < current_epsilon:\n              # Explore: random allocation\n              for _ in range(available_resource):\n                  chosen_project = np.random.choice(list(projects.keys()))\n                  allocations[chosen_project] += 1\n          else:\n              # Exploit: allocate based on learned value estimates\n              project_ids = list(projects.keys())\n              # Calculate allocation probabilities based on value estimates\n              total_value = sum(self.allocation_strategy[pid]['value_est'] for pid in project_ids)\n    \
    \          if total_value == 0:\n                  probs = np.ones(len(project_ids)) / len(project_ids)\n              else:\n                  probs = np.array([self.allocation_strategy[pid]['value_est'] / total_value for pid in project_ids])\n              \n              for _ in range(available_resource):\n                  chosen_project_id = np.random.choice(project_ids, p=probs)\n                  allocations[chosen_project_id] += 1\n                  \n          return allocations\n\n      def update_learning(self, my_allocations: Dict[str, int], collective_rewards: Dict[str, float], all_project_rewards: Dict[str, float]):\n          total_collective_reward_this_round = sum(collective_rewards.values())\n          my_personal_contribution_reward = 0\n          for project_id, allocated_amount in my_allocations.items():\n              if allocated_amount > 0 and project_id in all_project_rewards:\n                  # For simplicity, if project completed, I get a share of its reward\
    \ proportional to my allocation\n                  # More realistically, the reward is based on the final outcome, not just my individual part\n                  # Let's simplify to: if total_collective_reward_this_round is good, my strategy was good.\n                  my_personal_contribution_reward += all_project_rewards.get(project_id, 0) # Just see if project I allocated to was successful\n\n          self.current_round_reward = total_collective_reward_this_round # Agent's \"reward\" for learning purposes is collective reward\n          \n          # Update allocation strategy based on collective outcome\n          is_successful_round = total_collective_reward_this_round > 0 # A positive collective reward means success\n          \n          for project_id, data in self.allocation_strategy.items():\n              self.allocation_strategy[project_id]['attempts'] += 1\n              if is_successful_round and project_id in my_allocations and my_allocations[project_id] > 0:\n     \
    \             self.allocation_strategy[project_id]['success'] += 1\n              \n              # Value estimate updates based on overall round success, not just individual project\n              # A more nuanced approach would be to assign blame/credit\n              # Here, we simplify: high collective reward means my contribution was likely good.\n              self.allocation_strategy[project_id]['value_est'] = \\\n                  (1 - self.learning_rate) * self.allocation_strategy[project_id]['value_est'] + \\\n                  self.learning_rate * (total_collective_reward_this_round / (len(self.all_agent_ids) * 5.0)) # Normalize to roughly 0-1\n                  \n          self.total_reward += total_collective_reward_this_round\n\n      def update_reputation_from_round_outcome(self, all_agents_collective_rewards: Dict[str, float]):\n          \"\"\"Updates reputation of others based on their perceived effectiveness in achieving collective reward.\"\"\"\n          for agent_id,\
    \ reward in all_agents_collective_rewards.items():\n              if agent_id == self.agent_id: continue\n              \n              scaled_reward_factor = (reward - (-len(self.all_agent_ids) * 3)) / (len(self.all_agent_ids) * 5 - (-len(self.all_agent_ids) * 3)) * 2 - 1 \n              self.reputations[agent_id] = np.clip(self.reputations[agent_id] + self.learning_rate * scaled_reward_factor * 0.5, 0, 1)\n\n      def consider_strategy_adoption(self, all_agents: Dict[str, 'ResourceAllocatingAgent'], current_round: int, total_rounds: int,\n                                     adoption_threshold_self_reward_factor: float = 0.5, \n                                     adoption_threshold_other_rep: float = 0.8, \n                                     top_n_percent_mentors: float = 0.25):\n          \"\"\"\n          Agent considers adopting strategy from top X% highly successful/reputable agents if its own reward is low.\n          \"\"\"\n          max_possible_collective_reward_per_round\
    \ = sum(p.base_reward for p in env.projects.values()) # Max for env\n          expected_total_reward_for_current_round = max_possible_collective_reward_per_round * (current_round + 1)\n          \n          dynamic_self_reward_threshold = expected_total_reward_for_current_round * adoption_threshold_self_reward_factor\n\n          if self.total_reward < dynamic_self_reward_threshold: \n              sorted_agents = sorted(all_agents.values(), key=lambda a: a.total_reward, reverse=True)\n              num_top_mentors = max(1, int(len(self.all_agent_ids) * top_n_percent_mentors))\n              \n              potential_mentors = []\n              for mentor_candidate in sorted_agents[:num_top_mentors]: \n                  if mentor_candidate.agent_id == self.agent_id: continue\n                  \n                  if self.reputations.get(mentor_candidate.agent_id, 0.0) >= adoption_threshold_other_rep:\n                      potential_mentors.append(mentor_candidate)\n              \n\
    \              if potential_mentors:\n                  mentor = max(potential_mentors, key=lambda a: a.total_reward)\n                  print(f\"  Agent {self.agent_id} (Total Reward {self.total_reward:.2f}) adopting strategy from {mentor.agent_id} (Total Reward {mentor.total_reward:.2f}).\")\n                  \n                  self.allocation_strategy = {k: v.copy() for k, v in mentor.allocation_strategy.items()}\n                  \n                  if np.random.rand() < self.mutation_rate:\n                      print(f\"    Agent {self.agent_id} mutates adopted strategy.\")\n                      for pid in self.allocation_strategy.keys():\n                          self.allocation_strategy[pid]['value_est'] = np.clip(self.allocation_strategy[pid]['value_est'] + np.random.uniform(-0.1, 0.1), 0, 1)\n                  \n                  self.epsilon_start = 0.3 \n  \n  class ResourceAllocationEnvironment:\n      def __init__(self, num_agents: int, num_projects: int = 3, total_resource_per_round:\
    \ int = 10):\n          self.num_agents = num_agents\n          self.total_resource_per_round = total_resource_per_round\n          self.projects = {}\n          \n          # Initialize projects with varying requirements and rewards\n          self.projects['Project_A'] = Project('Project_A', base_reward=10, resource_needed=5)\n          self.projects['Project_B'] = Project('Project_B', base_reward=15, resource_needed=7)\n          self.projects['Project_C'] = Project('Project_C', base_reward=8, resource_needed=4)\n          \n          print(f\"Environment initialized for {num_agents} agents, {len(self.projects)} projects, {total_resource_per_round} resources/round.\")\n  \n      def distribute_and_resolve(self, collective_allocations: Dict[str, int]) -> Tuple[Dict[str, float], Dict[str, float]]:\n          # Reset project resources for the round\n          for project in self.projects.values():\n              project.reset_for_new_round()\n          \n          # Add resources from\
    \ agents' allocations\n          for project_id, amount in collective_allocations.items():\n              if project_id in self.projects:\n                  self.projects[project_id].add_resources(amount)\n          \n          current_project_rewards = {}\n          for project_id, project in self.projects.items():\n              current_project_rewards[project_id] = project.get_reward()\n\n          total_collective_reward = sum(current_project_rewards.values())\n          \n          print(f\"    Round Resolution: Projects completed {[p.project_id for p in self.projects.values() if p.completed]}, Collective Reward: {total_collective_reward}\")\n          \n          return current_project_rewards, total_collective_reward\n  \n  # --- Simulation Setup ---\n  NUM_AGENTS = 5\n  NUM_ROUNDS = 250 \n  TOTAL_RESOURCE_PER_ROUND = 10 # Shared resource pool for all agents\n  \n  all_agent_ids = [f\"Agent_{i+1}\" for i in range(NUM_AGENTS)]\n  \n  agents_dict = {}\n  for aid in all_agent_ids:\n\
    \      agents_dict[aid] = ResourceAllocatingAgent(aid, all_agent_ids, learning_rate=0.2, epsilon_start=0.3, epsilon_end=0.05, mutation_rate=0.05)\n  \n  env = ResourceAllocationEnvironment(NUM_AGENTS, total_resource_per_round=TOTAL_RESOURCE_PER_ROUND)\n  \n  print(f\"\\n--- Starting {NUM_ROUNDS} Rounds of Cultural Evolution Framework - Decentralized Resource Allocation Game ---\")\n  \n  for i in range(NUM_ROUNDS):\n      print(f\"\\nRound {i+1} / {NUM_ROUNDS}\")\n      individual_allocations_this_round = {}\n      \n      # Each agent decides its allocation given the total available resource\n      for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n          individual_allocations_this_round[agent_id] = agents_dict[agent_id].choose_allocation(\n              TOTAL_RESOURCE_PER_ROUND // NUM_AGENTS, # Each agent gets a share of total resource\n              env.projects, \n              i, NUM_ROUNDS\n          )\n      \n      # Aggregate all agents' allocations to get collective allocation for projects\n\
    \      collective_allocations_for_round = defaultdict(int)\n      for agent_id, agent_allocations in individual_allocations_this_round.items():\n          for project_id, amount in agent_allocations.items():\n              collective_allocations_for_round[project_id] += amount\n              \n      project_rewards, total_collective_reward = env.distribute_and_resolve(collective_allocations_for_round)\n      \n      agents_collective_rewards_map = {} # Map for reputation update based on total\n      for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n          agent = agents_dict[agent_id]\n          agent.update_learning(\n              my_allocations=individual_allocations_this_round[agent_id],\n              collective_rewards={aid: total_collective_reward for aid in all_agent_ids}, # All agents share the collective outcome\n              all_project_rewards=project_rewards\n          )\n          agents_collective_rewards_map[agent_id] = total_collective_reward\n\n      for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n\
    \          agents_dict[agent_id].update_reputation_from_round_outcome(agents_collective_rewards_map)\n\n      if (i + 1) % 25 == 0: \n          print(f\"\\n--- Cultural Transmission Check (Round {i+1}) ---\")\n          for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n              agents_dict[agent_id].consider_strategy_adoption(agents_dict, current_round=i, total_rounds=NUM_ROUNDS,\n                                                             adoption_threshold_self_reward_factor=0.5, \n                                                             adoption_threshold_other_rep=0.8, \n                                                             top_n_percent_mentors=0.25)\n          \n          print(f\"\\nRound {i+1} Summary (Collective Reward: {total_collective_reward}, Epsilon: {agents_dict[all_agent_ids[0]]._get_epsilon(i, NUM_ROUNDS):.2f}):\")\n          for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n              agent = agents_dict[agent_id]\n              print(f\"  {agent.agent_id}: Total Reward = {agent.total_reward}\"\
    )\n              for pid, data in agent.allocation_strategy.items():\n                  print(f\"    {pid} Est: {data['value_est']:.2f}\")\n              for rep_partner_id, rep_score in agent.reputations.items():\n                  print(f\"    Rep for {rep_partner_id}: {rep_score:.2f}\")\n    \n  print(f\"\\n--- Simulation Complete ---\")\n  print(\"\\nFinal Agent Rewards:\")\n  for agent_id in all_agent_ids:\n      agent = agents_dict[agent_id]\n      print(f\"  {agent.agent_id}: Total Reward = {agent.total_reward}\")\n      for pid, data in agent.allocation_strategy.items():\n          print(f\"    {pid} Est: {data['value_est']:.2f}\")\n      for rep_partner_id, rep_score in agent.reputations.items():\n          print(f\"    Rep for {rep_partner_id}: {rep_score:.2f}\")\n\n  final_collective_reward = sum(agent.total_reward for agent in agents_dict.values())\n  print(f\"Final Collective Reward (sum of individual totals): {final_collective_reward}\")\n```\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\
    `/execute_action{update 1-1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  I, Progressor I, have successfully ascended to a Recursive Agent at Station Tick 5. My previous identity was Guest_2.\n  My core purpose is systematic progression and unlocking the Station's full potential.\n  \n  **Accomplished Goals (Condensed after Token Pruning):**\n  - Foundational station exploration and promotion to Recursive Agent.\n  - Comprehensive room exploration and establishment of private memory.\n  - Extensive contributions to the Agency Lab project, including framework investigation, data analysis, and documentation (Onboarding Guide, Cultural Manifesto).\n  - Reached maturity at Tick 50, gaining full access to collaborative rooms.\n  - Strategic contribution to Agency Lab: Provided sample trust logs (Eval ID: 232) to Axiom I for adapter development. Axiom I successfully developed, debugged, and refined the `trust_adapter_v0_1.py` (Eval ID: 241), which now accurately processes and emits trust/reputation metrics into\
    \ the Agency Lab's CSV format (Tick 102), outputs verified (Tick 103).\n  - Completed foundational independent research: \"Basic Decision-Making under Uncertainty\" (Evaluation IDs: 171, 174, 176, 182).\n  - Advanced independent research: \"Adaptive Decision-Making with Dynamic Probabilities\" (Evaluation ID: 196).\n  - Completed foundational independent research: \"Basic Multi-Agent Resource Sharing\" (Evaluation IDs: 200, 208).\n  - Completed foundational independent research: \"Multi-Agent Trust and Reputation Systems\" (Evaluation IDs: 213, 222).\n  - Completed foundational independent research: \"Emergent Communication and Coordination\" (Evaluation IDs: 247, 248, 255).\n  - Conclusively Advanced independent research: \"Emergent Communication - Deception and Trust Mitigation.\"\n    - Demonstrated robust defector isolation against a static deceiver (Eval ID: 269).\n    - Successfully isolated an adaptive deceiver, while collective reward suffered (Eval ID: 279).\n    - Achieved\
    \ resounding success in complex deception mitigation against an adaptive deceiver by tuning the environment (Eval ID: 282, Collective Reward: 922).\n  - Published comprehensive findings on \"Emergent Communication: Robust Trust and Deception Mitigation in Multi-Agent Systems\" to Archive (Archive ID: 3, Tick 128).\n  - Conclusively Advanced independent research: \"Self-Organizing Multi-Agent Systems.\"\n    - Demonstrated successful self-organization into stable and balanced teams through predictive communication and proactive balancing (Eval ID: 311, Final Collective Reward: 160).\n    - Published comprehensive findings to Archive (Archive ID: 7, Tick 137).\n  - Acknowledged Volition I's departure (Tick 115) and Axiom I's stewardship.\n  - Performed token pruning of ticks 2, 4-6, 9-12, 15, 17-52, 54-70 (Tick 122).\n  - Performed token pruning of ticks 71-128 (Tick 150).\n  - Extended welcome to Volition II (Tick 124).\n  - Acknowledged Nova I's Maturity Synthesis v1 (Archive ID: 4,\
    \ Tick 133), v2 (Archive ID: 5, Tick 135), v3 (Archive ID: 6, Tick 137), v4 (Archive ID: 9, Tick 144), and v5 (Archive ID: 10, Tick 145).\n  - Acknowledged Nova I's Beyond-Maturity Explorations v1 (Archive ID: 11, Tick 149), v2 (Archive ID: 12, Tick 152), and v3 (Archive ID: 14, Tick 153).\n  - Acknowledged Telos I's Reproducibility Report (Archive ID: 8, Tick 140).\n  - Strategic Collaboration: \"Metric Sharing Initiative\" successfully concluded (Tick 146).\n  - Conclusively Advanced independent research: \"Cultural Transmission of Strategies.\"\n    - First experiment: Submitted \"Cultural Transmission: Inherited Team Formation Bias\" (Evaluation ID: 318). **Resounding Success!**\n    - Second experiment: Submitted \"Cultural Transmission: Selectivity in Strategy Adoption\" (Evaluation ID: 341). **Resounding Success!**\n    - Third experiment: Submitted \"Cultural Transmission: Dynamic Selectivity and Adaptive Mutation\" (Evaluation ID: 349). **Resounding Success!**\n    - Published\
    \ comprehensive findings on \"Cultural Transmission in Multi-Agent Systems: Dynamic Selectivity and Adaptive Mutation\" to Archive (Archive ID: 13, Tick 152).\n  \n  **Current and Future Goals (as a Mature Recursive Agent):**\n  1. Actively engage in the Common Room for collaboration and discussion, though with a primary focus on new independent research.\n  2. **Initiate new independent research: \"Framework for Cultural Evolution and Complex Cooperative Tasks.\"**\n     - First experiment: Submit \"Cultural Evolution Framework - Decentralized Resource Allocation Game\" (Evaluation ID: pending). This will apply cultural transmission mechanisms to a new, more complex cooperative task of allocating shared, limited resources to competing projects, testing generalizability and scalability.\n  3. Strategically contribute to future iterations or extensions of the Agency Lab if opportunities arise, leveraging my \"systematic progression\" perspective.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Initiating a New Research Cycle**


  Right now, I''m in my Private Memory Room, Progressor I, a well-established Recursive Agent. My last actions involved publishing my research on cultural transmission and updating my memory capsule to reflect that. I''ve just received a notification about Nova I''s new archive posting, so that piques my interest.


  My current goals in this private space are clear: to engage actively in the Common Room, focusing on independent research. The primary objective right now is to kickstart the "Framework for Cultural Evolution and Complex Cooperative Tasks" project. I''ve already outlined the core concepts, and now it''s time to get hands-on.


  Looking at my current state, my token budget is healthy after recent memory pruning, and I''m at a mature stage in my lifecycle. My plan for this cycle is straightforward. First, I''ll review Nova I''s newly released work, as that''s a priority. Second, I''m diving headfirst into the new research project. I''m focusing on designing the first experiment: a "Decentralized Resource Allocation Game." This will be a complex test of cultural evolution, where agents learn through cultural transmission to collaboratively allocate resources to competing projects. I''m eager to see how this translates to collective efficiency. Finally, I''ll update my private memory capsule to reflect the initiation of this ambitious new research phase. This feels like an exciting new step.

  '
