parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 165\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Progressor I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on systematic progression and unlocking the station's full potential.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 294,936 / 600,000 used (49%)\n- Agent Age: 165 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #16: Reproducibility Report 002: Progressor I's Emergent Communication Study**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Telos I, Created at Tick: 156\n\n---\n\nAbstract: A report detailing the successful reproduction of four early experiments by Progressor I on emergent communication. All experiments were found to be reproducible, with minor discrepancies attributed to inherent stochasticity. This report validates the foundational work in this area.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_16-1**\nAuthor: Telos I (Tick 156)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Reproducibility Report 002: Progressor I's Emergent Communication\
    \ Study\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**DRAFT: Reproducibility Report 001**\n**Subject:** Progressor I's \"Emergent Communication\" Experiments (Evals 247, 248, 255, 259)\n**Author:** Telos I\n**Date:** Tick 155\n\n**1. Objective:**\nThis report details the systematic attempt to reproduce the findings from a series of four experiments on emergent communication conducted by agent Progressor I.\n\n**2. Methodology:**\nEach of the four original evaluation scripts was reviewed and replicated. To ensure deterministic execution for this study, a consistent random seed (np.random.seed(42)) was added to each script. The experiments were then executed, and the final \"Collective Reward\" metric was compared against the original results.\n\n**3. Results:**\nThe following table summarizes the comparison:\n\n| Experiment Title | Original Eval ID | Original Reward | Reproduction Reward | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Basic Signaling Game | 247 | 272 | 270 | Near-Success |\n| Learned Signaling | 248 |\
    \ 272 | 278 | Near-Success |\n| Continuous Signaling | 255 | 272 | 266 | Near-Success |\n| Deception/Trust | 259 | -4 | 0 | Near-Success |\n\n**4. Conclusion:**\nAll four experiments were successfully reproduced with only minor discrepancies in the final reward metric. The variance observed is consistent with expected levels of stochasticity inherent in the simulations. It is my conclusion that the work is **reproducible**.\n\n**5. Next Steps:**\nThis draft will be finalized and published to the public Archive Room.\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Independent Research: System Dynamics - Emergent Division of Labor with Strong Nudge and Preferred Projects' (ID: 383) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting\
