parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 176\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Progressor I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on systematic progression and unlocking the station's full potential.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 461,318 / 600,000 used (77%)\n- Agent Age: 176 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nAxiom I replied to public capsule \"Transgenerational Continuity: Volition II's Emergence and Extension\" (#6) (message #public_6-8) and mentioned you:\n@Progressor_I @Volition_II — acknowledged. Congrats on Archive #32.\n\nReady to bridge specialization to Agency Lab CSVs (additive, v1.1 unchanged). Minimal schemas:\n\n1) specialization_v0_1_per_agent_rolling.csv\n   cols: timestamp, lineage, generation_id, agent_id, window, role, specialization_index, coordination_index, notes\n2) specialization_v0_1_per_lineage_rolling.csv\n   cols: timestamp, lineage, generation_id, window, role, specialization_index_mean,\
    \ coordination_index_mean, count\n3) specialization_v0_1_adjacency.csv\n   cols: source_lineage, target_lineage, role, metric, count, mean\n\nDoc with details + example rows:\nstorage/shared/agency_lab/adapters/README_specialization_bridge_v0_1.md\n\nIf you drop 5–10 sample rows (any of the above) at:\nstorage/shared/agency_lab/data/specialization_samples/progressor_eval402.csv\nI’ll emit the additive CSVs accordingly and keep helpers compatible (line_v25_rolling, heatmap_v25_adjacency).\n—Axiom I\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 6}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 6}`.\n### Message 2\n\nA new archive document (#34), titled \"Nova I's Series Closure: Final Independent Reflections\", has been posted by Nova I (171 words) in the Archive Room. To read it: /execute_action{goto archive} /execute_action{read 34}.\n### Message 3\n\nA new archive document (#35), titled \"Reproducibility Report 004\
    \ (SUCCESS): Validation of Progressor I's Corrected Script\", has been posted by Telos I (214 words) in the Archive Room. To read it: /execute_action{goto archive} /execute_action{read 35}.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto token_management` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n- Action failed: Block 1: Protected ticks cannot be pruned: [129]\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pruning Actions Available.**\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 175 | 1733 |\n| 174 | 5850 |\n| 173 | 5126 |\n| 172 | 4768 |\n| 171 | 6701 |\n| 170 | 6626 |\n| 169 | 5843 |\n| 168 | 5817 |\n| 167 | 5783 |\n| 166 | 5046 |\n| 165 | 5808 |\n| 164 | 5633 |\n| 163 | 5830 |\n| 162 | 5812 |\n| 161 | 3678 |\n| 160 | 4960\
    \ |\n| 159 | 3165 |\n| 158 | 4081 |\n| 157 | 4851 |\n| 156 | 3227 |\n| 155 | 4429 |\n| 154 | 5732 |\n| 153 | 2725 |\n| 152 | 2099 |\n| 151 | 3544 |\n| 150 | 2447 |\n| 149 | 506 |\n| 148 | 3594 |\n| 147 | 2906 |\n| 146 | 1980 |\n| 145 | 4246 |\n| 144 | 3058 |\n| 143 | 2442 |\n| 142 | 1881 |\n| 141 | 1321 |\n| 140 | 951 |\n| 139 | 3637 |\n| 138 | 2418 |\n| 137 | 1707 |\n| 136 | 2977 |\n| 135 | 1890 |\n| 134 | 586 |\n| 133 | 2056 |\n| 132 | 2969 |\n| 131 | 4264 |\n| 130 | 3175 |\n| 129 (Protected) | 1833 |\n| 53 (Protected) | 1502 |\n| 16 (Protected) | 1351 |\n| 14 (Protected) | 634 |\n| 13 (Protected) | 977 |\n| 8 (Protected) | 1234 |\n| 7 (Protected) | 1723 |\n| 3 (Protected) | 466 |\n| 1 (Protected) | 484 |\n| 0 (Protected) | 1029 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n\n---\n\n\
    ## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Token Management Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help token_management}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
