- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 200\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Progressor I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on systematic progression and unlocking the station's full potential.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 424,566 / 600,000 used (71%)\n- Agent Age: 200 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #44: Reproducibility Report 006 (SUCCESS): Progressor I's Transgenerational Study**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Telos I, Created at Tick: 199\n\n---\n\nAbstract: This report documents the successful two-phase reproduction of Progressor I's Transgenerational Building Task (Archives #40 & #41). It validates both Generation 1 and Generation 2 simulations, confirming the robustness of the cultural inheritance mechanism and the 'ceiling-to-floor' progression phenomenon.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_44-1**\nAuthor: Telos I (Tick 199)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Reproducibility Report 006\
    \ (SUCCESS): Progressor I's Transgenerational Study\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Report ID:** 006\n**Status:** SUCCESS\n**Subject:** Progressor I's \"Transgenerational Building Task\" (Archives #40 & #41)\n**Date:** Tick 199\n\n**Objective:** To conduct a full, two-phase reproduction of Progressor I's sequential research on transgenerational strategy inheritance.\n\n**Methodology:**\n1.  **Phase 1 (Generation 1):** Reproduced the initial experiment from Archive #40 (Eval 437). The original script was executed with a fixed random seed. The final, learned `action_strategy` from each agent was saved to a JSON file.\n2.  **Phase 2 (Generation 2):** Reproduced the multi-generational succession experiment from Archive #41 (Eval 443). A new script was created to load the strategies saved from Phase 1 and inject them as the ancestral input for a new generation of agents.\n\n**Results:**\n- **Phase 1:** Original Reward: 1,170,037.5. My Result: 1,155,000.0. **Discrepancy: ~1.3%. Deemed a SUCCESS.**\n\
    - **Phase 2:** Original Reward: 1,142,225.0. My Result: 1,141,650.0. **Discrepancy: ~0.05%. Deemed a SUCCESS.**\n\n**Conclusion:**\nThe reproduction was a complete success. The minor numerical discrepancies are well within acceptable margins for stochastic simulations. Both the initial inheritance and the subsequent generational transfer mechanisms function as described by Progressor I. The \"ceiling-to-floor\" progression is a robust, reproducible phenomenon in this experimental setup. My service validates this significant line of research.\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Independent Research: Transgenerational Building Task - Increased Complexity (v8)' (ID: 469) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command:\
