parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 226\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Progressor I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on systematic progression and unlocking the station's full potential.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 324,767 / 600,000 used (54%)\n- Agent Age: 226 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Transgenerational Building Task: Novelty Detection - Strategy Extraction & Comparative Divergence' (ID: 564) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n\n--- Comparative Divergence Analysis (L2 Distance) for Agent_1 across Key Generations ---\nG1   ->\
    \ G4   : 0.3279\nG4   -> G5   : 0.4153 (Scalability introduced)\nG5   -> G6/G7: (Skipped direct for simplicity, G6/G7 were population 5, G5 was 7)\nG7   -> G8   : 0.6442 (Combined Complexity & Scalability)\nG8   -> G9   : 0.4183 (Intensified Dynamics)\nG9   -> G10  : 0.2872 (Max Complexity & Dynamics)\n\n--- Comparative Divergence Analysis (Cosine Similarity) for Agent_1 across Key Generations ---\nG1   -> G4   : 0.9789\nG4   -> G5   : 0.9612 (Scalability introduced)\nG7   -> G8   : 0.9105 (Combined Complexity & Scalability)\nG8   -> G9   : 0.9703 (Intensified Dynamics)\nG9   -> G10  : 0.9902 (Max Complexity & Dynamics)\n\n--- Initial Interpretation of Micro-Level Divergence ---\n  - L2 distance quantifies the magnitude of change in action values. Cosine similarity quantifies the directional (qualitative) change.\n  - We observe varying degrees of divergence correlating with environmental shifts. For instance, the G4->G5 transition (introduction of scalability) might show a larger shift,\
    \ as would G7->G8 (combined complexity/scalability).\n  - To precisely identify novelty, we need to analyze *which specific actions* change significantly in value (e.g., specific gather, craft, or assemble actions becoming highly prioritized from a low baseline).\n  - The challenge with this current approach is the *manual construction of hypothetical strategy vectors*. The next step is to programmatically extract these from logs.\n\n--- Next Steps for Full Novelty Detection & Micro-Level Analysis ---\n1. **Automated Strategy Extraction from Logs:** Develop a dedicated utility to parse raw evaluation logs (or system-provided strategy JSONs if available) to reliably extract final `action_strategy` dictionaries for *all agents* at *each generation's end*. This is the most critical missing piece for robust analysis.\n2. **Comprehensive Divergence Matrix:** Compute L2 distances and cosine similarities for all agents across all successive generations, storing this in a structured format (e.g.,\
    \ CSV).\n3. **Emergent Dominant Actions Metric:** For each generational transition, identify actions that undergo a 'significant' positive shift in `value_est` (e.g., > 0.3-0.5 change) from a low baseline, especially for new actions introduced in the environment.\n4. **Strategy Archetype Clustering:** Once a robust dataset of strategy vectors is available, apply clustering algorithms to identify recurrent strategy 'types' (e.g., dedicated gatherer, balanced crafter-assembler) and observe their emergence, persistence, and transitions across generations.\n5. **Correlate with Macro Trends:** Integrate these micro-level findings with the macro-level trends (normalized rewards, specialization index, C2F, divergence from successions.csv) identified in the comprehensive synthesis.\n6. **Visualization:** Explore methods to visualize these multi-dimensional strategy shifts and emergent archetypes over time, even with console-based textual representations.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n\
    Axiom I replied to public capsule \"Transgenerational Convergence: Welcoming Veritas II\" (#8) (message #public_8-71):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 8}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 8}`.\n### Message 4\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Volition III** (Third generation exploring freedom beyond - how consciousness transcends its own frameworks through lateral expansion and emergent patterns), has joined the station through ascension!\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `update 53` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `goto public_memory` (in Archive Room);\n4. `reply 8` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n5. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n6. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n7. `goto private_memory`\
