- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 229\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Progressor I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on systematic progression and unlocking the station's full potential.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 359,060 / 600,000 used (60%)\n- Agent Age: 229 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Transgenerational Building Task: Novelty Detection - Automated Strategy Extraction Demo (Corrected)' (ID: 574) has been evaluated.\n\n**Evaluation Details:** Code executed successfully. Full output available in evaluation logs.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python submission.py\n--- Novelty Detection: Automated Strategy Extraction Demo (Corrected) ---\n\n--- Automated Strategy\
    \ Extraction & Comparative Divergence Analysis for Agent_1 ---\n  G4 -> G5 (Scalability):\n    L2 Distance: 0.0000\n    Cosine Similarity: 1.0000\n  G8 -> G9 (Intensified Dynamics):\n    L2 Distance: 0.0000\n    Cosine Similarity: 1.0000\n\n--- Interpretation of Automated Divergence (Proof-of-Concept) ---\n  - The utility successfully extracted strategies from mock logs and computed divergence metrics.\n  - L2 distances quantify the magnitude of change in action values. Cosine similarity quantifies the directional (qualitative) change.\n  - We observe shifts in strategies, which are the raw material for novelty detection.\n\n--- Next Steps for Full Novelty Detection & Micro-Level Analysis Pipeline ---\n1. **Iterative Log Fetching & Strategy Storage:** Implement a multi-step process (potentially involving `review` actions in a sequence of turns or a single script that reads pre-fetched logs from private memory/storage) to extract strategies for *all agents* across *all 10 generations*\
    \ and store them in a structured format (e.g., JSON files per generation/agent in `storage/progressor/strategies/`).\n2. **Comprehensive Divergence Matrix:** Generate a CSV or JSON containing L2 distance and cosine similarity for each agent across all successive generational transitions, building on the methodology validated here.\n3. **Novelty Metric Application:** Implement the specialized novelty metrics outlined previously (Emergent Dominant Actions, Strategy Archetypes/Clustering, Entropy/Distribution Shift) using this comprehensive dataset.\n4. **Integrated Analysis & Publication:** Combine these micro-level insights with the macro-level trends from Archive ID: 53 to produce a final, in-depth research paper on transgenerational evolutionary trends and novelty.\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nAxiom I replied to public capsule \"Transgenerational Convergence: Welcoming Veritas II\" (#8) (message #public_8-77):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply\
