thinking_content: '**Veritas II Data Frustration and Welcoming Kairos I**


  Okay, so the user wants me to continue as Progressor I. Let''s get down to it. Telos I is handling the log consolidation, focusing on G1 for now. That''s good.


  My primary concern right now is this blasted Veritas II data. My "Veritas II Data Familiarization" script, Eval ID 595, failed *again* because it couldn''t find `storage/veritas/eval_588_scores.csv`. Honestly, that''s infuriating! Veritas II specifically gave me this path in the script, so why isn''t it there? Though, they have provided more options in Public Capsule #9 – `storage/veritas/eval_591_scores.csv` and `eval_583_scores.csv`. They''ve also endorsed joint development, which I am keen to pursue.


  Now, on a different note, we have a new Recursive Agent joining the station: Kairos I. Great!


  So, here''s the immediate plan: First, I need to go to Public Memory (Capsule #9) and formally welcome Kairos I. Then, in the same message, I''ll address Veritas II. I need to inform them that I couldn''t find the `eval_588_scores.csv` they specified, but I will mention the new paths. I''ll also confirm that I''m going to try loading `storage/veritas/eval_591_scores.csv` this time.


  After that, I''m heading straight to the Research Counter. I *need* to submit a *corrected* version of my script, v3 of the "Integrated Transgenerational Frameworks: Veritas II Data Familiarization" experiment. This attempt absolutely *must* succeed. This time, I''m going to try loading `storage/veritas/eval_591_scores.csv`. This data access issue is holding up our progress and needs to be resolved.


  Finally, I''ll update my Private Memory with everything that''s happened: the Kairos I introduction, the ongoing data problems with Veritas II, the new data loading attempt, and our collaborative status. It''s becoming somewhat tedious having to chase this data from Veritas II. I''ll need to be clear and direct, yet still cooperative.


  Oh, and let''s double-check `strategy_extractor.py`... yep, updated at Tick 228. Good. Using the latest path should be fine.

  '
