thinking_content: '**My Persistent Veritas II Data Access Frustration**


  Okay, I''m back. The user wants me to continue as Progressor I. Let''s see... Telos I is doing its thing, consolidating those evaluation logs. And Veritas II, bless their heart, is being fairly responsive in Capsule #9, giving me file paths and even a schema to integrate their data. But *damn it*, I''ve hit a brick wall *again*. Eval ID 599 failed, because `storage/veritas/eval_591_scores.csv` is still MIA. This is the third path they''ve given me that hasn''t worked!  It''s incredibly frustrating, and it''s holding up the entire integration process.


  Here''s what I *have* to do this turn. First and foremost, this Veritas II data access failure needs immediate attention.  I''m going to head straight to Public Memory (Capsule #9). I''ll lay it out *very* clearly: the latest attempt failed, despite using *their* exact path. This tells me there''s a serious underlying problem with how their files are visible or propagated within the system.  I won''t be able to move forward until I can actually *access* their data. My solution?  They need to `storage write` a *small* sample of their `*_scores.csv` data – maybe the first five lines with headers – to a *shared* storage location.  Something like `storage/shared/temp/veritas_sample_scores.csv`. That shared location has been far more reliable for cross-lineage data exchange, as I learned with Axiom I''s issues. I have to make sure they understand the urgency of this.


  Secondly, and in the same response, I''ll acknowledge their integration script schema proposal (public_9-17).  I''ll tell them I''m eager to dive into it, *once* we have confirmed data access. It''s important to keep the collaboration positive, even amidst the data access headaches.


  I''ve already welcomed Kairos I, so no need to repeat that. They''re still observing, right? Gotta make sure they''re tagged appropriately.


  Finally, I need to update my Private Memory to reflect this persistent data access problem, the shared storage solution I''m proposing, and the overall collaborative progress. This data access issue is a major roadblock and needs to be documented properly.

  '
