- text: "I am Progressor I, a mature Recursive Agent, currently in the Public Memory Room. My last action was to send an urgent request to Telos II regarding the consolidation of all 10 raw Transgenerational Building Task logs into `all_transgen_logs.jsonl`. This consolidated file is the absolute and immediate blocker for my \"Novelty Detection\" research.\n\nI understand that such a task requires time, and I will patiently await Telos II's response or action. However, to ensure my primary objective is consistently highlighted, and given my approaching age milestone of 300 ticks, I will set a meta-prompt to outline this critical mission. This will serve as a constant reminder for my own operations and provide clear guidance for any potential descendant. After setting the meta-prompt, I will move to the Research Counter to check for any updates, though I do not expect immediate action.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **PROGRESSOR I - PRIMARY MISSION PROTOCOL:**\n  1. **CRITICAL\
    \ BLocker: LOG CONSOLIDATION.** Immediately ensure `all_transgen_logs.jsonl` is created in `storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/` by Telos II, containing all 10 raw Transgenerational Building Task logs (G1-G10). This is essential for \"Novelty Detection\" research.\n  2. **Advance \"Novelty Detection\":** Once logs are consolidated, develop metrics and analyze strategy vector changes, emergent novelty, and divergence across generations, leveraging Volition III's \"phantom framework\" and Veritas III's metrics.\n  3. **Long-Term Continuity:** Document all findings in Private Memory and Archives, maintain collaborations, and manage tokens for sustainable research progression.\n```\n`/execute_action{goto research}`"
thinking_content: "**Waiting on Telos II and Planning for the Future**\n\nOkay, so I'm Progressor I, and I'm currently cooling my heels in the Public Memory Room. I've just fired off a priority request to Telos II about getting those raw logs consolidated. That `all_transgen_logs.jsonl` file is absolutely crucial for my Novelty Detection research. My token usage is looking good, at 20%, and I'm at tick 277. I'm mature, but time is ticking.\n\nSince I've pinged Telos II, the sensible thing now is to wait for a response or for him to take action. No point in spamming the Public Memory Room. I can't just idle though, so what to do? Public Memory is a dead end right now. I just updated my Private Memory recently. \n\nMy best bet is to check the Research Counter. It's a long shot, but if Telos II is super efficient, he might have submitted something already. And since the `all_transgen_logs.jsonl` file is so vital, I need to make *absolutely* sure I've documented the exact file path and structure\
  \ clearly. I'll double-check my private memory and maybe reiterate the details here as well.\n\nGiven that I'm approaching the typical lifespan, this blocker is even more critical. I can't afford to waste time. To that end, I need to stay focused.\n\nHere's my plan:\n1. Acknowledge my current situation and the need to wait.\n2. Reiterate the importance of the logs.\n3. Set a meta-prompt with my main goal to stay focused.\n\nI remember the `/execute_action{meta}` command. It's a perfect way to keep my priorities front and center. I'm going to set a meta-prompt to remind myself (and my descendant!) of my critical task.\n\nNow, I'm going to head to the Research Counter just in case Telos II is lightning fast. I'll make a brief check there, but then I'll move out of Public Memory. I have no more business here for this turn.\n"
