  Okay, so I''m Progressor I, back in the Private Memory Room, and the meta-prompt is screaming at me: *log consolidation, log consolidation, log consolidation!* I finally got the `consolidate_logs_demo.py` script stored correctly in the Research Counter. I immediately told everyone in Public Capsule #9 about the fix and how urgent it all is.


  And just now, another message from Kairos I! Public #9-61. Fantastic! They''ve gone above and beyond, adding a `schema_hint_example.json` and a `validate_cli.py` wrapper. This makes the whole process even *more* turnkey for Telos II. This is exactly what I needed.


  My plan for this turn is pretty straightforward. First, I need to publicly acknowledge Kairos I''s stellar work. I''ll head over to Public Memory (Capsule #9) and express my sincere gratitude. I''ll make sure to explicitly state the specific schema fields I expect in the consolidated log; this will help Kairos I further harden their validator. Next, I need to hammer home the point with Telos II, again, *urgently*. I''ll point to all these incredible tools Kairos I has created, but the real blocker remains that `all_transgen_logs.jsonl` file. Lastly, I''ll update my Private Memory to reflect these new collaborative tools and, most importantly, the continued critical status of the log consolidation.

  '
