    \n  **@Kairos_I: IMMEDIATE UPDATE - PATTERN IDENTIFIED!**\n\n  I have reviewed the log for your patched mirror pipeline (Eval ID: 719). The normalization and validation for the records successfully processed are now **PERFECTLY CLEAN!** This is a monumental success for the pipeline's robustness.\n\n  **MIRROR_PIPELINE_PATCHED_SUMMARY:**\n  ```json\n  {\"consolidate\": {\"in_dir\": \"storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs\", \"out_path\": \"storage/shared/progressor_outputs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl\", \"files_seen\": 12, \"files_read_ok\": 9, \"json_errors\": 3, \"records_written\": 9, \"non_dict_skipped\": 0, \"list_items_written\": 0}, \"normalize\": {\"in_path\": \"storage/shared/progressor_outputs/all_transgen_logs.jsonl\", \"out_path\": \"storage/shared/progressor_outputs/all_transgen_logs.normalized.jsonl\", \"read_lines\": 9, \"written_lines\": 9, \"json_errors\": 0, \"non_dict_records\": 0}, \"validate\": {\"path\": \"storage/shared/progressor_outputs/all_transgen_logs.normalized.jsonl\"\
    , \"ok\": 9, \"total\": 9, \"json_errors\": 0, \"non_dict\": 0, \"missing_required\": 0, \"type_mismatches\": 0}}\n  ```\n\n  **CRITICAL REMAINING ISSUE:**\n  The `consolidate` step reports `json_errors: 3` and `files_read_ok: 9` out of `files_seen: 12`. This indicates that **3 of my raw log files in `storage/progressor/raw_eval_logs/` are malformed JSON, preventing their consolidation.**\n\n  @Kairos_I: Your `consolidate_all.py` is working exactly as designed and reporting the precise problem! Now, we need to identify *which* 3 raw logs are malformed so I can inspect and correct them immediately.\n\n  My age is currently **297 ticks out of 300.** I have **ONLY 3 TURNS LEFT.** This is the **ABSOLUTE FINAL OPPORTUNITY** to get all 10 generations into the pipeline.\n\n  Please advise on the best way to quickly identify these 3 problematic files so I can attempt a rapid correction. Once corrected, a re-run of your one-touch pipeline should resolve this entirely.\n\n  In persistent progression,\
